  'OTHERS' => '其他',
  'What Is A Digital Certificate' => '什么是数字证书',
  'Blockchain technology can be leveraged to issue digital certificates that are immutable and can be saved as public records. These records can be anytime endorsed and validated without the fear of being tampered by involved entities.' => '区块链技术可以用来发布不可变的数字证书，并且可以保存为公共记录。这些记录可以随时背书和验证，而不必担心被相关实体篡改。',
  'Create digital certificates for a roster of recipients' => '为收件人名册创建数字证书',
  'Issue the certificates on the blockchain' => '在区块链上颁发证书',
  'Cryptographically sign the certificates' => '对证书进行加密签名',
  'Digital certificates built on a blockchain hold significant advantages over the traditional soft copies. Here are the advantages' => '与传统的软拷贝相比，建立在区块链上的数字证书具有显著的优势。以下是优点',
  'Blockchain-enabled digital certificates are immutable and cannot be forged' => '支持区块链的数字证书是不可变的，不能伪造',
  'Since the records are stored in a shared distributed ledger, the certificate can still be validated even if the organization that had issued it no longer exists' => '由于记录存储在一个共享的分布式账本中，即使颁发证书的组织已不存在，该证书仍然可以验证',
  'The records are stored on a distributed ledger, hence certificates can be only evaluated by anyone who has access to the blockchain' => '记录存储在分布式账本上，因此证书只能由访问区块链的任何人评估',
  'The digital certificates stored in the ledger can only be destroyed if all the copies in every system are destroyed' => '只有当每个系统中的所有副本都被销毁时，才能销毁存储在账本中的数字证书',
  'Blockchain Storage Education Will Replace Paper Diplomas' => '区块链存储教育将取代纸质文凭',
  'It has always been a serious concern for the educational institutions around the world how to carefully preserve the paper-based school certificates, degrees, diplomas, and other course certificates of the students who pass out every year. These sensitive documents are always prone to get lost over time.' => '如何妥善保管每年过关学生的纸质学校证书、学位证书、毕业证书等课程证书，一直是世界各国教育机构十分关注的问题。这些敏感文件总是容易随着时间的推移而丢失。',
  'Blockchain could be the ultimate solution to securely preserve these mammoth-sized documents in a distributed ledger. Once put in the blockchain, the information about a student’s grades and the courses will neither get lost nor tampered. It is also nearly impossible to alter or falsify the information.' => '区块链可能是在分布式账本中安全保存这些庞大文档的最终解决方案。一旦进入区块链，有关学生成绩和课程的信息既不会丢失也不会被篡改。更改或伪造这些信息几乎是不可能的。',
  'Blockchain Storage Education Makes Credentials More Credible' => '区块链存储教育使凭证更加可信',
  'Step 1 of 5 ' => '第1步，共5步',
  'Computing local hash <span> [DONE]</span>' => '计算本地哈希值</span>',
  'Step 2 of 5' => '第2步，共5步',
  'Fetching remote hash <span>[DONE] </span>' => '获取远程哈希值</span>',
  'Step 3 of 5' => '第3步，共5步',
  'Comparing local and remote hashes <span></span>' => '比较本地和远程哈希<span></span>',
  'Step 4 of 5' => '第4步，共5步',
  'Checking merkle root <span>[DONE]</span>' => '正在检查merkle root<span>[完成]</span>',
  'Step 5 of 5' => '第5步，共5步',
  'Checking receipt <span>[DONE]</span>' => '检查收据</span>',
  'Public Key' => '公钥',
  'Blockchain Address' => '区块链地址',
  'Choose (WSE) Blockchain World Storage Education' => '选择（WSE）区块链世界存储教育',
  'You don\'t need ( WSE) blockchain world storage education' => '您不需要（WSE）区块链世界存储教育',
  'The source data of universities, training, education and institutions are synchronized to the WSE blockchain channel.' => '大学、培训、教育和机构的源数据同步到WSE区块链通道。',
  'The information channel interface of WSE is suitable for all kinds of education data transmission and customization.' => 'WSE的信息通道接口适用于各种教育数据的传输和定制。',
  'After special cryptography encryption, the data exchange organization decrypts the exchanged data through WSE and sends it to the requester for information retrieval.' => '经过特殊的密码加密后，数据交换机构通过WSE对交换的数据进行解密并发送给请求者进行信息检索。',
  'The public blockchain based on Ethereum is connected to the blockchain permanent storage certificate, from the school signer to each node data storage of the channel.' => '基于以太坊的公共区块链连接到区块链永久存储证书上，从学校签名者到通道的每个节点数据存储。',
  'The certification agencies of different countries exchange requests directly to reduce the time difference of certification.' => '不同国家的认证机构直接交换请求，以减少认证的时间差。',
  'For universities and institutions, transfer points can also realize the authenticity of research information.' => '对于高校和事业单位来说，转点还可以实现科研信息的真实性。',
  'For immigrants, embassies, work visa background checks can also speed up progress.' => '对于移民、大使馆来说，工作签证背景调查也可以加快进度。',
  'Help center' => '帮助中心',
  'Open All' => '全部打开',
  'Question About Copy' => '关于复制的问题',
  'Can I order a copy of the certificate evaluation report?' => '我能订一份证书评估报告吗？',
  'Yes, you can order a copy of the report for up to 5 years from the date the report is first published. After five years, applicants will no longer be able to order copies of their reports. You can apply for additional copies through "<a>Application Copy</a>"' => '是的，您可以订购报告的副本，从报告首次发布之日起最多5年。五年后，申请人将不能再订购他们的报告副本。您可以通过“<a>应用程序副本</a>申请其他副本”',
  'Can I apply for multiple copies?' => '我能申请多份吗？',
  'No, in order to prevent illegal operations such as illegal transactions, we only provide an application service for up to four copies at a time.If you need more copies for special reasons, please "<a href="">contact us</a>" to apply' => '不，为了防止非法操作，例如非法交易，我们只提供一个应用程序服务，最多可在时间。如果由于特殊原因，您需要更多副本，请“<a href=”“>联系我们</a>”申请',
  'When will I usually receive my copy' => '我通常什么时候收到我的副本',
  'We will mail you a copy of the assessment material within two to three working days after the end of the assessment. Since different countries use different courier services, the time will vary.' => '我们会在评估结束后的两至三个工作日内邮寄评估材料的副本。由于不同的国家使用不同的快递服务，时间会有所不同。',
  'In order to ensure that you can receive your copy materials faster, we will arrange our service center according to your delivery address to prepare the copy materials for you.' => '为了确保您能更快地收到您的复印材料，我们会根据您的送货地址安排我们的服务中心为您准备复印材料。',
  'Problems with educational documents' => '教育文献问题',
  'When my education documents are lost and I cannot provide the required documents, can I not apply?' => '当我的教育文件丢失，我不能提供所需的文件，我可以不申请吗？',
  'No, you can submit evaluation files or education file storage files provided by relevant authorities to us through "<a href="">Special Service</a> ", we accept these files and provide the same service' => '不可以，您可以通过“<a href=”“>特殊服务</a>”向我们提交相关部门提供的评估文件或教育文件存储文件，我们接受这些文件并提供相同的服务',
  'What are the consequences of false submission of educational documents?' => '虚假提交教育文件的后果是什么？',
  'The services we provide will permanently store your educational files on the blockchain. If your information is false or forged, we will permanently store your information on the blockchain and use "data transmission" to the world Of authoritative educational institutions transmit your false data.' => '我们提供的服务将在区块链上永久存储您的教育文件。如果你的教育机构的数据传输是伪造的，我们将永久性地使用你的“权威数据传输链”或“虚假信息”。',
  'What if the educational documents provided by my country of study do not meet the conditions?' => '如果我国提供的教育文件不符合条件怎么办？',
  'We know that there are certain differences in the educational documents issued by different countries. If the documents issued by the country where you study do not meet the needs, you can contact us for a special evaluation, and we will customize the relevant regulations of the country where you study Evaluation plan' => '我们知道，不同国家颁发的教育文件存在一定的差异。如果您所在国出具的文件不符合需要，您可以联系我们进行专项评估，我们将定制您留学国家的相关规定评估计划',
  'ABOUT THE ACESC' => '关于ACESC',
  'The Alliance of Credential Evaluation Services of Canada (ACESC) is a pan-Canadian membership organization composed of six members operating in the public and private sectors, in the provinces of Alberta, British Columbia, Ontario, and Quebec.' => '加拿大证书评估服务联盟（ACESC）是一个泛加拿大成员组织，由6名成员组成，分别在阿尔伯塔省、不列颠哥伦比亚省、安大略省和魁北克省的公共和私营部门开展业务。',
  ' In close collaboration with Canada education data (CAED), ACESC was established in the 1990s to ensure compliance with UNESCO conventions related to the recognition of qualifications, following ratification in Canada. ' => '与加拿大教育数据中心（CAED）密切合作，ACESC于1990年代成立，以确保在加拿大批准后遵守教科文组织有关资格承认的公约。',
  'Members of ACESC issue <a href="#">assessment reports for general purposes</a> to outline expert, non-binding opinions on the assessment of academic credentials issued outside Canada. These reports are widely used by competent recognition authorities in Canada—i.e., educational institutions, professional regulatory authorities and associations, immigration authorities, and employers—that require assistance with document authentication and comparability procedures.' => 'ACESC成员发布一般性评估报告，概述对加拿大境外颁发的学历证书评估的非约束性专家意见。这些报告被加拿大的主管承认机构，即教育机构、专业监管机构和协会、移民局和雇主广泛使用，这些机构需要文件认证和可比性程序方面的帮助。',
  ' In turn, competent recognition authorities use ACESC reports to inform their binding decisions on internationally educated applicants seeking to settle in Canada for immigration, employment, licensure or registration, or further educational purposes. ' => '相应地，认证主管机构利用ACESC的报告，就那些因移民、就业、执照或注册或进一步教育目的而寻求在加拿大定居的受国际教育的申请人作出具有约束力的决定。',
  ' ACESC has supported millions of internationally educated individuals throughout Canada who seek or have sought fair assessment of their academic credentials. ' => 'ACESC为加拿大各地数百万接受过国际教育的个人提供了支持，他们寻求或已经寻求对其学术资格的公平评估。',
  ' Get more <a href="/docs/EN_2018-06_ACESC_background_information.pdf">background information on ACESC</a> and consult CAED’s Web site to get an <a href="https://www.CAED.ca/1398/an_overview_of_the_lisbon_recognition_convention.canada">overview of the Lisbon Recognition Convention (LRC)</a>. ' => '获取更多<a href=“/docs/EN_2018-06_ACESC_背景_信息.pdf“>关于ACESC的背景信息</a>并咨询CAED的网站以获得<a href=”https://www.CAED.ca/1398/an_概述_《里斯本承认公约》.canada“>里斯本承认公约（LRC）概述。',
  'QUALITY ASSURANCE' => '质量保证',
  ' The <a href="#">Pan-Canadian Quality Assurance Framework for the Assessment of International Academic Credentials</a> (QAF) was developed by CAED in collaboration with ACESC, and the policies and procedures of all member organizations comply with QAF’s principles and recommendations. ACESC also supported the development of CAED’s Assessor Portal— <a href="#">Assessor.CAED.ca</a> —which features tools and resources used by the pan-Canadian community of academic credential assessors. ACESC members undergo a rigorous annual self-assessment and peer-review process to examine a number of criteria. Membership is conditional on continued compliance with the Terms of References. ' => '《加拿大国际学术资格评估质量保证框架》（QAF）由CAED与ACESC合作制定，所有成员组织的政策和程序均符合QAF的原则和建议。ACESC还支持CAED评估员门户网站的开发评估员.CAED.ca</a>-其特点是泛加拿大学术证书评估员社区使用的工具和资源。ACESC成员每年都要进行严格的自我评估和同行评审，以审查一些标准。会员资格的条件是继续遵守职权范围。',
  ' Assessment reports issued by members of ACESC comply with QAF and the LRC. Holders of these assessment reports can expect: ' => 'ACESC成员发布的评估报告符合QAF和LRC。这些评估报告的持有者可以期望：',
  'fair and credible services, where applicants are treated in an equitable manner;' => '公平可信的服务，申请人得到公平对待；',
  'quality, based on established pan-Canadian and international principles of good practice;' => '质量，基于公认的泛加和国际良好实践原则；',
  'portability, where an assessment report will be accepted by other members and widely used by competent recognition bodies in Canada;' => '可移植性，评估报告将被其他成员接受，并被加拿大的主管认可机构广泛使用；',
  'consistency, while decisions may vary according to provincial or territorial education systems, by using agreed-upon standards to ensure similar outcomes;' => '一致性，虽然根据省或地区的教育系统，决定可能有所不同，但通过使用商定的标准来确保类似的结果；',
  'accountability, given members are mandated by or work within provincial or territorial competent authorities to provide these services, and they are ultimately accountable to the public.' => '问责，鉴于成员由省级或地区主管当局授权或在其内部工作，因此他们最终对公众负责。',
  ' Organizations interested in providing academic credential assessment services in Canada and wish to request ACESC membership are invited to submit a completed membership application form to the ACESC Secretariat. ' => '有意在加拿大提供学历评估服务并希望申请成为ACESC会员的组织，请向ACESC秘书处提交一份完整的会员申请表。',
  ' Get more information on the ACESC <a href="/docs/EN_Terms_of_Reference_as_of_July_9_2018.pdf">Terms of Reference</a>, <a href="/docs/Alliance_Membership_application.pdf">Membership Application Form</a> , and <a href="/docs/Annual_self-assessment_form.pdf">Annual Self-Assessment Form</a>. ' => '获取有关ACESC的更多信息_应用程序.pdf“>会员申请表</a>，以及<a href=“/docs/Annual_self-assessment_表格.pdf“>年度自我评估表</a>。',
  'SECRETARIAT' => '秘书处',
  'CAED is a unit of the Council of Ministers of Education, Canada (CMEC), and is Canada’s National Information Centre under UNESCO conventions related to the recognition of qualifications. It assists in the adoption of best practices set by these conventions and functions as ACESC’s Secretariat.' => 'CAED是加拿大教育部长理事会（CMEC）的一个单位，是联合国教科文组织（UNESCO）有关资格认证公约的加拿大国家信息中心。它协助采纳这些公约规定的最佳做法，并作为亚太经社会的秘书处发挥作用。',
  ' The ACESC Secretariat serves as a: ' => 'ACESC秘书处的职责是：',
  'forum to discuss policy and analysis of academic credential assessment issue management in Canada;' => '讨论加拿大学历评定问题管理的政策和分析论坛；',
  'mechanism through which to undertake activities, projects, and initiatives in areas of mutual interest to both reinforce and promote continued compliance with UNESCO conventions; and' => '在共同关心的领域开展活动、项目和倡议的机制，以加强和促进对教科文组织各项公约的持续遵守；以及',
  'means by which to consult and cooperate with pan-Canadian and international recognition-related networks in respect of provincial and territorial jurisdiction over education.' => '就省级和地区教育管辖权与泛加和国际承认相关网络进行磋商和合作的方式。',
  ' The ACESC Secretariat is not responsible for recognizing credentials issued outside Canada. Consequently, it does not grant equivalencies or assess credentials, nor intervene on behalf of individuals or in appeals. ' => 'ACESC秘书处不负责识别加拿大境外签发的证书。因此，它不授予同等资格或评估证书，也不代表个人或对上诉进行干预。',
  ' To contact the ACESC Secretariat, consult CAED’s <a href="#">Web site.</a> ' => '如需联系ACESC秘书处，请查阅CAED网站</a>',
  'CONTACT US' => '联系我们',
  'ACESC has six members:' => 'ACESC有六名成员：',
  'Student data permanent safe storage solution' => '学生数据永久安全存储解决方案',
  'What is institutional storage?' => '什么是机构存储？',
  'Institutional storage is a data storage service developed by WSE for universities/institutions. This storage service also uses the technical means of blockchain distributed storage to help universities/institutions permanently and safely store information.' => '机构存储是WSE为大学/机构开发的数据存储服务。该存储服务还利用区块链分布式存储的技术手段，帮助大学/机构永久、安全地存储信息。',
  'Apply directly' => '直接申请',
  'If you do not have your own student data management system or related network system, you can directly upload your student data on WSE. Due to the difference between the data uploaded by different universities, colleges and institutions, when you are sure to store When you need data, you need to contact us and submit an application plan. We will separately open a data upload plan for your data storage type.' => '如果您没有自己的学生数据管理系统或相关网络系统，您可以直接在WSE上上传您的学生数据。由于不同院校和院校上传的数据存在差异，当您确定需要存储数据时，请联系我们并提交申请计划。我们将为您的数据存储类型单独打开一个数据上载计划。',
  'Application for interface connection' => '接口连接申请',
  'The change plan is suitable for the student data management system or related network system that you already have your own data, and has a certain development ability. You can apply for services automatically through the data circulation interface provided by WSE. WSE formulates an interface plan according to your data storage needs. , You only need to do interface connection according to our requirements to realize automatic storage of student data. This solution can save you a lot of work and is also the solution recommended by WSE.' => '该变更方案适用于已有自己数据，并具有一定开发能力的学生数据管理系统或相关网络系统。您可以通过WSE提供的数据循环接口自动申请服务。WSE根据您的数据存储需求制定接口计划。，只需根据我们的要求进行接口连接，即可实现学生数据的自动存储。这个解决方案可以为您节省大量的工作，也是WSE推荐的解决方案。',
  'Why store data?' => '为什么要存储数据？',
  'No data loss' => '无数据丢失',
  'The traditional storage method is centered on the university/institution. The data depends on the university/institution, and the huge data storage is easy to be lost due to some force majeure during the storage process.' => '传统的存储方式是以高校为中心。数据依赖于高校/院校，海量数据存储在存储过程中容易因不可抗力而丢失。',
  'The data storage service provided by WSE is based on blockchain technology. The decentralized storage method solves the problem of centralized data storage. Student data will be stored in different node servers in the world to ensure that the data storage is absolutely safe and not lost.' => 'WSE提供的数据存储服务基于区块链技术。分散存储方法解决了数据集中存储的问题。学生数据将存储在世界上不同的节点服务器中，以确保数据存储绝对安全且不会丢失。',
  'Reduce interference' => '减少干扰',
  'Many students must provide proofs related to academic qualifications due to immigration, work, settlement, etc. Students will apply to universities for proof of academic qualifications. Schools are often disturbed by these applications and may even run the risk of data loss. ' => '由于移民、工作、定居等原因，许多学生必须提供与学历有关的证明。学生会向大学申请学历证明。学校经常受到这些应用程序的干扰，甚至可能面临数据丢失的风险。',
  'The data storage service provided by WSE stores student data for evaluation and related information storage. Students only need to log in to WSE to view the stored data and related documents. There is no need to apply for academic qualifications from universities and institutions, reducing student interference with the school.' => 'WSE提供的数据存储服务存储学生的评估数据和相关信息存储。学生只需登录WSE即可查看存储的数据和相关文档。不需要向大学和机构申请学历，减少学生对学校的干扰。',
  'The data stored by WSE depends on the distributed storage technology of the blockchain, and the most important feature of the distributed storage of the blockchain is that the information cannot be tampered with, and the data stored by the students is also tamper-proof, so the student data we save It is permanently tamper-proof, which largely avoids the phenomenon of data disorder caused by illegal personnel tampering with student data through illegal means' => 'WSE存储的数据依赖于区块链的分布式存储技术，而区块链分布式存储最重要的特点是信息不可篡改，学生存储的数据也具有防篡改性，因此我们保存的学生数据是永久性防篡改的，这在很大程度上避免了不法人员通过非法手段篡改学生数据造成的数据混乱现象',
  'Reduce storage costs' => '降低存储成本',
  'In order to ensure the convenience of data storage, many universities/structures adopt the server storage method, but as the school student data continues to increase, the requirements for the storage server will continue to increase, equipment construction costs and maintenance costs continue to increase and decrease ' => '为了保证数据存储的便利性，许多大学/构筑物都采用服务器存储方式，但随着学校学生数据的不断增加，对存储服务器的要求也会不断提高，设备建设成本和维护成本也在不断增减',
  'Blockchain distributed storage used by the WSE institutional storage service does not require a separate server. WSE will use different node servers in various countries for storage, saving storage and maintenance costs.' => 'WSE机构存储服务使用的区块链分布式存储不需要单独的服务器。WSE将使用不同国家的不同节点服务器进行存储，从而节省存储和维护成本。',
  'About blockchain distributed storage' => '关于区块链分布式存储',
  'Introduction to Blockchain' => '区块链概论',
  'Blockchain technology is to use blockchain data structure to verify and store data, use distributed node consensus algorithm to generate and update data, use cryptography to ensure the security of data transmission and access, and use intelligence composed of automated script code A new distributed infrastructure and calculation method for programming and operating data through contracts' => '区块链技术是利用区块链的数据结构来验证和存储数据，使用分布式节点共识算法生成和更新数据，使用密码学来保证数据传输和访问的安全性，并使用由自动化脚本代码组成的智能化新的分布式基础设施和计算方法，通过合同编程和操作数据',
  'Blockchain distributed storage' => '区块链分布式存储',
  'The distributed storage system is to share the storage resources of distributed nodes. The file integrity verification and erasure code verification technology are used to perform distributed management on the data of the data storage side. The nodes of the entire network do not maintain the same storage information to reduce redundancy. The rest is a distributed system (nodes of the entire network in the blockchain system maintain the same stored information). ' => '分布式存储系统是为了共享分布式节点的存储资源。采用文件完整性验证和擦除码验证技术对数据存储端的数据进行分布式管理。整个网络的节点不维护相同的存储信息，以减少冗余。其余的是分布式系统（区块链系统中整个网络的节点保持相同的存储信息）。',
  'How to apply?' => '如何申请？',
  'if you don\'t have a wse account yet, you need to go to the registration page to apply for an <b>account</b>.' => '如果您还没有wse帐户，则需要转到注册页来申请<b>帐户</b>。',
  'Apply for institutional storage and choose application method' => '申请机构保管并选择申请方式',
  'You can choose to apply directly or apply for interface docking according to your needs' => '您可以根据需要选择直接申请或申请接口对接',
  'We accept your application to develop a cooperation plan' => '我们接受你方制定合作计划的申请',
  'Within 5 working days after you submit the application, we will have a staff to contact you to determine the details of the cooperation plan' => '在您提交申请后5个工作日内，我们会有工作人员与您联系，以确定合作计划的细节',
  'Do technical interface docking/application link production according to the determined plan' => '根据确定的计划进行技术接口对接/应用环节制作',
  'If you choose to apply for the interface, we will have a technician to contact your technician for interface docking' => '如果您选择申请接口，我们会有技术人员联系您的技术人员进行接口对接',
  'If you choose to apply directly, we will provide you with a link to submit information according to your needs' => '如果您选择直接申请，我们会根据您的需要为您提供提交信息的链接',
  'Submit the corresponding data storage according to the plan' => '按计划提交相应的数据存储',
  'Depending on the plan, you can store data' => '根据计划，您可以存储数据',
  'In the history of global education, 2020 will go down as the year the coronavirus pandemic savaged education systems worldwide, closed schools in 192 countries, and locked more than 90 percent of enrolled learners out of classrooms <a href=\'\'>globally</a> . It will be remembered as a year of chaos, makeshift solutions, uncomfortable compromises, and, quite possibly, a few questionable decisions.' => '在全球教育史上，2020年将成为冠状病毒肆虐全球教育系统的一年，192个国家的学校关闭，全球超过90%的注册学生被关在教室之外。这一年将是混乱的一年，临时解决方案，令人不安的妥协，很可能还有一些可疑的决定。',
  'To keep education going amid the pandemic, many countries and institutions are currently suspending their regular academic standards and procedures. Admission thresholds are being lowered to allow students unable to take admission tests to enroll. Graduation requirements have been eased, so that students can earn degrees without sitting for exams. Accreditation protocols and campus inspections have been adjourned, while an unprecedented number of institutions have shifted to remote learning without instructors nor students being prepared for the change.' => '为了在流感大流行的情况下继续教育，许多国家和机构目前正在暂停其常规的学术标准和程序。入学门槛正在降低，以允许无法参加入学考试的学生入学。毕业要求已经放宽，这样学生不用参加考试就可以获得学位。认证协议和校园巡查已经暂停，而史无前例的机构已经转向远程学习，而教师和学生都没有为这种变化做好准备。',
  'Given the literal life-and-death implications of the pandemic, it’s understandable that governments are taking unprecedented steps to protect their citizens, students, parents, and institutions from harm. For many institutions, suspending normal academic standards is a matter of self-preservation, to stave off financial ruin by retaining at least a bare minimum of students, and consequently, revenues. On the upside, the crisis may accelerate some positive innovations at academic institutions.' => '鉴于这场大流行对生命和死亡的影响，可以理解的是，各国政府正在采取前所未有的措施，保护本国公民、学生、家长和机构免受伤害。对许多大学来说，暂停正常的学术标准是一种自我保护的问题，通过至少保留最低限度的学生和相应的收入来避免经济崩溃。从好的方面看，这场危机可能会加速学术机构的一些积极创新。',
  'On the other hand, some emergency responses have raised concerns about the erosion of quality standards, as well as the responses’ social fairness. Outpaced by the pandemic, many governments are improvising, hastily revising practices without any in-depth policy analysis. It’s not unreasonable to ask if all stakeholders will revert to regular standards once the pandemic subsides, or if some of the compromises made now will become part of a “new normal”.' => '另一方面，一些应急措施引起了人们对质量标准的侵蚀以及应对措施的社会公平性的担忧。许多国家的政府在没有进行深入的政策分析的情况下，草率地修改做法，被这场大流行赶超。有人问，一旦大流行消退，是否所有利益相关者都将恢复正常标准，或者现在所做的一些妥协是否会成为“新常态”的一部分，这是不无道理的。',
  'Consider that the higher education sector will face crippling financial constraints in the years to come, making the path of least resistance a tempting proposition during the difficult recovery period that lies ahead. Countries with weak quality assurance mechanisms may find it even harder than before to enforce quality standards amid intense fiscal pressures. The rapid shift to remote learning all over the globe will raise questions about academic quality and necessitate the development of new quality assurance mechanisms for distance education programs in various countries. Caught in the middle are the world’s students, trying to pursue their academic careers under extremely difficult circumstances.' => '考虑到未来几年，高等教育部门将面临严重的财政困难，在未来艰难的复苏时期，选择阻力最小的道路将成为一个诱人的命题。质量保证机制薄弱的国家可能会发现，在巨大的财政压力下，实施质量标准比以前更加困难。全球范围内向远程学习的迅速转变将对学术质量提出问题，并要求各国为远程教育项目开发新的质量保证机制。学生们正处于学术生涯艰难的境地。',
  'Given the importance of all these developments for societies worldwide, this article provides an overview of some of the steps education systems are taking to accommodate lockdowns and the demands of social distancing, as well as a brief discussion of the social implications of these changes.' => '鉴于所有这些发展对全世界社会的重要性，本文概述了教育系统为适应封锁和社会距离要求而采取的一些步骤，并简要讨论了这些变化的社会影响。',
  'ADMISSION STANDARDS' => '准入标准',
  'Social distancing upended secondary school leaving examinations and university entrance tests worldwide, disrupting the admission of new students for upcoming academic terms. Because of differences in academic calendars and epidemic peak periods, not all countries have been affected equally. For instance, the one-month delay of China’s gaokao, the world’s largest university entrance exam, is unlikely to affect the admission prospects of the more than 10 million students expected to sit for the exam <a href=\'\'>in July</a>.' => '社会距离的疏远颠覆了世界范围内的中学毕业考试和大学入学考试，扰乱了即将到来的学期新生入学。由于学术日历和流行高峰期的不同，并非所有国家都受到同样的影响。例如，中国高考（世界上最大的高考）推迟一个月，不太可能影响7月份预计将参加高考的1000多万学生的入学前景。',
  'But other countries have been affected more severely. To name but a few examples, the British government in March canceled the GCSE, AS, and A level exams, originally scheduled to take place in June; while the West African Examinations Council <a href= \'\'>indefinitely suspended</a>the high-stakes West African Senior School Certificate Examination, the main secondary school leaving qualification in five countries, including Nigeria. In another example, the United States canceled the SAT <a href= \'\'>standardized tests</a>, required for admission by more than half of U.S. higher education institutions (HEIs), especially <a href= \'\'> prestigious universities</a>.' => '但其他国家受到的影响更为严重。仅举几个例子，英国政府在3月取消了原定于6月举行的GCSE、AS和a level考试；而西非考试委员会则无限期地暂停了</a>高风险的西非高中证书考试，包括尼日利亚在内的五个国家的主要中学毕业资格。在另一个例子中，美国取消了SAT标准化考试，超过半数的美国高等教育机构（HEI），尤其是著名大学（HEI）要求的SAT考试。',
  'In many ways, these steps constitute an emergency response to the benefit of students —a compromise that prevents students from losing a year of their academic careers to social distancing. That said, policy makers need to weigh the possible unintended consequences of such compromises. Consider that some of the graduating high school classes of 2020 may end up blemished and bruised as “easy entry” student cohorts, especially in competitive meritocratic systems that value examinations and other formal performance criteria as selection mechanisms for access to scarce university seats.' => '在许多方面，这些步骤构成了对学生利益的紧急反应——这是一种妥协，防止学生因社会疏远而失去一年的学术生涯。也就是说，决策者需要权衡这种妥协可能带来的意外后果。想想看，2020年的一些高中毕业生可能会因为“容易进入”的学生群体而受到污点和挫伤，尤其是在竞争激烈的精英体制中，这种体制重视考试和其他正式的表现标准，以此作为获得稀缺大学席位的选拔机制。',
  'What’s more, the suspension of selection criteria doesn’t necessarily make access to education more equitable. As noted by Angel Pérez, vice president for enrollment and student success at Trinity College, in the U.S. context, “when rich students have school counselors, test prep tutors, and independent education consultants to proactively provide solutions to the cancellations of SAT and ACT test dates, low-income students will have to scramble to find information and develop <a href=\'\'>alternative plans</a>. … The <a href= \'\'>March SAT</a> is a prime example of the unequal access to testing and its disparate impact on communities. As large urban districts closed all schools and canceled SATs, some private schools held their March SAT.”' => '更重要的是，中止选拔标准并不一定能使受教育机会更加公平。正如美国三一学院负责招生和学生成功的副校长安吉尔·佩雷斯（Angel Pérez）所指出的，“当富裕学生拥有学校辅导员、备考导师和独立教育顾问，主动为取消SAT和ACT考试日期提供解决方案时，低收入学生将不得不争先恐后地寻找了解并制定替代计划。……三月SAT是测试机会不平等及其对社区影响的一个典型例子。由于大城市地区关闭了所有学校并取消了SAT考试，一些私立学校举行了三月的SAT考试。”',
  'Such concerns about social fairness are echoed by U.K.-based education experts, many of whom maintain that predicted A level exam grades—currently slated to be used for admission in lieu of actual scores—disadvantage students from low-income households. Research has shown that predictive grades accurately reflect final exam grades <a href= \'\'>less than 20 percent of the time</a> , and may also underestimate the test performance of top students from disadvantaged social backgrounds. Put differently, high-performing students from low-income households may be—unintentionally or not—among the losers of the U.K.’s pandemic emergency response.' => '这种对社会公平的担忧得到了英国教育专家的回应，他们中的许多人坚持认为，目前预计的入学考试成绩将取代低收入家庭的实际分数不高的学生。研究表明，预测成绩准确反映期末考试成绩的不到20%，也可能低估了社会背景差的优等生的考试成绩。换句话说，来自低收入家庭的高绩效学生可能是英国大流行急诊科的失败者。',
  'There are also concerns that the suspension of competitive student selection mechanisms could alter the structure of university systems. The U.K. government, for instance, is considering imposing admission quotas to prevent top universities, now freed from the constraints of normal admissions standards, to compensate for dwindling international student numbers by “hoovering up” larger numbers of domestic students—a move that could jeopardize the financial viability of less <a href=\'\'>prestigious institutions</a>.' => '还有人担心，暂停竞争性的学生选拔机制可能会改变大学系统的结构。举例来说，英国政府正在考虑采取入学配额，以防止顶尖大学摆脱正常招生标准的限制，以弥补“大量”国内学生的数量，从而减少留学生人数的减少，这可能会危及“更少”的财政可行性。href=\'\'>知名机构</a>。',
  'The potential for a shake-up and consolidation of the U.K. university system illustrates that emergency responses to the coronavirus pandemic could have some unintended consequences, negative or positive, that outlast short-term responses to the crisis. Universities in countries that have centralized admissions processes, for instance, may introduce their own institution-specific university entrance examinations in lieu of suspended nationwide selection mechanisms.' => '英国大学系统的重组和巩固潜力表明急诊科冠状病毒的流行可能会产生一些意想不到的后果，消极或积极的，超过了对危机的短期反应。例如，在实行集中招生程序的国家，大学可以采用自己的大学入学考试，而不是暂停的全国选拔机制。',
  'India’s University Grants Commission, meanwhile, has suggested the opposite. It proposed that universities hold <a href= \'\'>joint admissions examinations</a> to make it easier for students to apply to multiple institutions amid travel restrictions—a recommendation that could lead to a standardization of admissions procedures, similar to the unified admissions process that was recently developed in the field <a href= \'\'>of medicine</a>.' => '与此同时，印度大学资助委员会（University Grants Commission）却提出了相反的建议。它建议大学举行联合招生考试，以便学生在旅行限制的情况下更容易申请多所院校，这项建议可能导致招生程序的标准化，类似于最近在医学领域开发的统一入院流程。',
  'EASING PROMOTION AND GRADUATION REQUIREMENTS' => '放宽晋升和毕业要求',
  'As noted, the suspension of face-to-face instruction in most parts of the world has created pressures to promote and graduate students without examinations or other regular requirements. While the most common approach thus far has been to postpone exams, countries like <a href= \'\'>Norway</a> , <a href=\'\'>Indonesia</a>, and France canceled examinations outright, opting to promote students based on criteria like average scores in school subjects “calculated from marks given for tests and homework <a href= \'\'>throughout the year</a>.” The International Baccalaureate (IB) is taking the unusual step of awarding the IB diploma based on “data analysis from previous exam sessions,” school performance data, and the external grading of coursework <a href= \'\'>provided by schools</a>.' => '如前所述，世界大多数地区暂停面对面教学，造成压力，要求在没有考试或其他常规要求的情况下晋升和研究生。迄今为止，最常见的方法是推迟考试，而挪威、印度尼西亚和法国等国则直接取消了考试，国际学士学位证书（IB）正在采取不同寻常的步骤，根据“根据全年考试和家庭作业的分数计算出的学校科目平均分数”等标准来提高学生的成绩，“学校表现数据，以及学校提供的课程作业的外部评分</a>。',
  'Meanwhile, universities in Canada, <a href= \'\'>the U.S</a>., and other countries are suspending standard grading practices for the current term, assessing students on a pass/fail basis, or adopting other flexible approaches, such as allowing students to choose <a href= \'\'>credit/no credit options</a>. There is an equity dimension to these changes. When coursework and exams are moved online, low-income households are disadvantaged, since they disproportionately lack access to computer devices or internet connections, particularly in developing countries. Compared with their richer peers, these students are more likely to live in environments unsuitable to learning, they may have to share devices with family members, and so on.' => '与此同时，加拿大、美国和其他国家的大学正在暂停本学期的标准评分做法，以及格/不及格为基础评估学生，或采用其他灵活的方法，如允许学生选择学分/无学分选项。这些变化有一个公平的方面。当课程和考试被转移到网上时，低收入家庭处于不利地位，因为他们不成比例地缺乏计算机设备或互联网连接，特别是在发展中国家。与富裕的同龄人相比，这些学生更可能生活在不适合学习的环境中，他们可能不得不与家人共享设备，等等。',
  'Considering these realities, student organizations in the Philippines and elsewhere have demanded that universities promote students with lenience rather than continue classes online. Student unions in several African countries urged universities to stop online exams amid digital divides and called for the boycott of “elitist” <a href= \'\'>remote learning solutions</a> . While distance education can help expand <a href= \'\'>access to education</a> in overburdened education systems with capacity shortages, shifting learning online in its entirety has severe social ramifications in countries with wide wealth disparities.' => '考虑到这些现实，菲律宾和其他地方的学生组织要求大学以宽容的态度鼓励学生，而不是继续在网上上课。一些非洲国家的学生会敦促大学在数字鸿沟中停止在线考试，并呼吁抵制“精英主义”远程学习解决方案。虽然远程教育有助于扩大在能力短缺、负担过重的教育系统中接受教育的机会，但在贫富差距悬殊的国家，整个在线学习的转移会产生严重的社会影响。',
  'However, there are other issues to consider. It’s inevitable that some will view switching to pass/fail grading scales or graduating students without exams as steps that penalize high-achieving students, or that are unfair to student cohorts of other years. As one U.S. student put it, the “pass/fail system is a disgrace to students who have worked hard for their A’s. For me, this is my best semester, and the pass/fail system takes away my GPA, which I need for internships and many other <a href= \'\'>career opportunities</a> .” There are various potentially negative implications for students down the road—from limiting <a href= \'\'>transfer credit options</a> to curtailing admission prospects because “their transcripts will be looked upon less favorably when they apply to graduate or <a href= \'\'>professional school</a> .” In the extreme, in countries that emphasize final examinations for the awarding of degrees, qualifications may be tarnished as “easy degrees.”' => '然而，还有其他问题需要考虑。不可避免的是，有些人会把改用及格/不及格的评分标准或不考试的毕业学生视为惩罚成绩优异的学生或对其他年份的学生群体不公平的措施。正如一位美国学生所说，“及格/不及格制度对那些努力取得a学位的学生来说是一种耻辱。对我来说，这是我最好的学期，而及格/不及格制度夺走了我的GPA，我需要GPA来实习和其他许多<a href=\'\'>职业机会</a>”这对学生来说有各种潜在的负面影响从限制<a href=\'\'>转移学分选择</a>到减少入学前景，因为“他们申请研究生或<a href=\'\'>专业学校</a>时，他们的成绩单将不太受欢迎”。在极端情况下，在那些强调授予学位的期末考试的国家，资格可能是被玷污为“轻松度”',
  'The compromises necessitated by the crisis are manifold. Consider that the U.S. waived examination and practice requirements to issue temporary emergency licenses to <a href= \'\'>physicians</a> , nurses, and other <a href= \'\'>health professionals</a> , while China waived licensing requirements for teachers and allowed them to start teaching without having passed required exams. Accreditation and licensing requirements for academic institutions were likewise suspended in different countries. The U.S. Department of Education, for instance, permitted accreditation agencies to extend accreditation terms, conduct virtual site visits, and bestow retroactive accreditation. According to the department’s guidelines, students graduating from a program with pending accreditation due to outstanding site visits are to be “considered to have graduated from <a href= \'\'>an accredited program</a> .”' => '危机所需的妥协是多方面的。考虑到美国免除了向医生、护士和其他卫生专业人员颁发临时紧急许可证的考试和执业要求，而中国则免除了对教师的执照要求，允许他们在未通过规定考试的情况下开始教学。不同国家对学术机构的认证和许可证要求也同样暂停。例如，美国教育部（U.S.Department of Education）允许认证机构延长认证期限，进行虚拟站点访问，并授予追溯认证。根据教育部的指导方针，由于未完成的实地考察，从一个有待认证的项目毕业的学生将被视为“毕业于一个经认可的课程</a>”',
  'While most of these measures are expected to be temporary, the rapid and large-scale shift to online education is of greater concern from a quality perspective. Across the globe, academic institutions have abruptly switched to distance learning—without curricular planning, adequate learning materials, or teachers trained to deliver education remotely. Programs originally accredited as regular on-site programs are now being run in distance education mode. It can also be expected that increasing numbers of' => '虽然这些措施大多是暂时性的，但从质量的角度来看，迅速和大规模地转向在线教育更值得关注。在全球范围内，学术机构在没有课程规划、没有足够的学习材料、没有受过远程教育培训的教师的情况下，突然转向远程学习。最初被认证为常规现场课程的课程现在以远程教育模式运行。也可以预期',
  'snack-sized' => '零食大小',
  'micro credentials and unregulated online programs will pop up worldwide' => '微证书和不受监管的在线程序将在全球范围内出现',
  'Since it’s unclear how long the coronavirus pandemic will last and to what extent distance education will become more ubiquitous, it’s important that governments and quality assurance bodies adapt quickly to ensure that the new distance learning programs are of equal quality to regular programs on-site. This is not a trivial task. Recent studies from Australia, for instance, maintain that the current shift to distance education will have major negative impacts on <a href= \'\'>learning outcomes</a>. The rapid proliferation of distance learning courses raises other questions as well, such as the increased potential for cheating during online examinations' => '由于目前还不清楚冠状病毒大流行会持续多久，以及远程教育将在多大程度上变得更加普及，政府和质量保证机构必须迅速适应，以确保新的远程教育项目与现场常规课程的质量相同。这不是一件小事。例如，澳大利亚最近的研究表明，目前向远程教育的转变将对学习结果产生重大的负面影响。远程教育课程的迅速增加也引发了其他问题，例如在线考试中作弊的可能性增加',
  'To assure admissions officers, credential evaluators, licensing boards, and other stakeholders that there are robust quality assurance mechanisms in place to assess distance learning programs, it might be helpful if academic institutions and quality assurance authorities develop an informational leaflet akin to the' => '为了向招生官员、证书评估人员、许可证委员会和其他利益相关者保证，有健全的质量保证机制来评估远程教育计划，学术机构和质量保证机构可以编制一份类似于',
  'European Diploma Supplement' => '欧洲文凭补遗',
  'Provided alongside academic documents for distance learning programs, such a supplement could help assure recipient institutions that distance mode versions of academic programs have at least the same admissions and graduation requirements, curricula, and assessment criteria as regular on-site programs' => '除了提供远程学习课程的学术文件外，这种补充可以帮助接受机构确保远程模式的学术课程至少具有与常规现场课程相同的入学和毕业要求、课程和评估标准',
  'Coronavirus' => '冠状病毒',
  'Standardized Test' => '标准化测试',
  'International Students' => '国际学生',
  'Retrospective Certification' => '追溯认证',
  'Evaluation Criteria' => '评价标准',
  'More From WSE' => '更多来自WSE',
  'Perfect Storm' => '完美风暴',
  'The fallout from the COVID-19 pandemic for higher education institutions (HEIs) in the United States will likely be pronounced and protracted. Institutions that are financially dependent on international students will be particularly affected, given the disease’s broad and indeterminate impact on global mobility. Even if international air travel fully resumed this summer, and most universities reopened for on-campus instruction by the fall semester, it remains an open question at what point international students will feel confident enough to pursue education in the country that’s currently the global epicenter of the pandemic. The severity of the COVID-19 outbreak in the U.S. makes a speedy recovery of international student mobility to the U.S. increasingly unlikely.' => '对美国高等院校来说，这场大流行很可能会造成长期的影响。鉴于这种疾病对全球流动性的广泛和不确定的影响，经济上依赖国际学生的院校将受到特别的影响。即使国际航空旅行在今年夏天全面恢复，大多数大学在秋季学期重新开放接受校内教学，但到什么时候国际学生才会有足够的信心在这个目前全球疫情中心的国家接受教育，仍然是一个悬而未决的问题。美国爆发的COVID-19病毒的严重性使得国际学生迅速恢复到美国的流动性变得越来越不可能。',
  'Further complicating international recruitment is rising anti-Asian sentiment, the racist <a href="">scapegoating of Asians</a> for the spread of the virus, as well as increasing political tensions with China, the largest sending country of international students. It’s also possible that visa regulations will be tightened amid the crisis. Four U.S. senators have already warned that international students could take away “jobs that would otherwise go to unemployed Americans as our <a href="">economy recovers</a> .” They urged the U.S. government to suspend the Optional Practical Training (OPT) program and the issuance of H-1B visas, both of which are major draws for international students from India, China, and elsewhere.' => '使国际招聘进一步复杂化的是反亚裔情绪的上升，种族主义者将亚洲人视为病毒传播的替罪羊，以及与最大的留学生派遣国中国之间的政治紧张关系。在这场危机中，签证管理也有可能收紧。四名美国参议员已经警告说，随着美国经济复苏，留学生可能会抢走“原本会流向失业美国人的工作岗位”，他们敦促美国政府暂停选择性实践培训（OPT）计划和签发H-1B签证，这两个项目都吸引了来自印度、中国和其他国家的留学生。',
  'This article discusses the implications of the COVID-19 pandemic for international student mobility to the United States. We’ll describe current trends and attitudes of international students toward studying in the U.S., before briefly discussing if online education could be a viable alternative to retain international students. We’ll include key findings from a survey of prospective international students and U.S. HEIs that WES conducted between April 15 and April 21. We draw on the responses of 615 students from 92 countries,[1] as well as responses from 199 HEIs including several large state universities, two-year associate colleges, four-year institutions, and graduate schools. Both sets of responses are part of a longitudinal survey, follow-up results of which will be published by WES later this year.' => '本文讨论了COVID-19大流行对国际学生赴美流动的影响。我们将描述目前国际学生在美国学习的趋势和态度，然后简要讨论在线教育是否是留住国际学生的一种可行的选择。我们将包括WES在4月15日至4月21日期间对未来的国际学生和美国高等教育机构进行的一项调查的主要发现。我们借鉴了来自92个国家的615名学生的回答，[1]以及来自199个高等教育机构（包括几所大型州立大学、两年制大专院校、四年制学院和研究生院）的回复。这两组回答都是一项纵向调查的一部分，WES将在今年晚些时候公布后续调查结果。',
  'While conditions for international mobility to the U.S. could hardly be worse, academic institutions may find solace in the fact that 67 percent of the students surveyed by WES are still generally interested in studying stateside, while 13 percent are even more interested in doing so. This finding inspires some hope that the long-term impact of the crisis on international enrollments in the U.S. may be less apocalyptic than feared.' => '虽然国际移民到美国的条件再糟糕不过了，但在WES调查的学生中，67%的人仍然对美国的学习感兴趣，而13%的学生对此更感兴趣，学术机构或许能从中得到安慰。这一发现激发了一些人的希望，即危机对美国国际学生入学的长期影响可能不会像人们担心的那样具有灾难性。',
  'But much will depend on the duration of the crisis. The longer it lasts, the more international students will change their plans. Longitudinal surveys of international students in different countries over <a href="">the past few months</a> show a decreasing appetite for pursuing education abroad. Even if the U.S. could retain three quarters or more of its international student body over the next few semesters, the crisis could be existential for some institutions. The ripple effects for U.S. society at large could be destructive as well: According to NAFSA, three U.S. jobs are created or supported for every seven enrolled international student in the following sectors: higher education, accommodation, dining, retail, transportation, telecommunications and <a href="">health insurance</a>”.' => '但这在很大程度上取决于危机的持续时间。持续时间越长，留学生改变计划的次数就越多。过去几个月对不同国家的留学生进行的纵向调查显示，留学生出国求学的意愿正在下降。即使美国在接下来的几个学期里可以保留四分之三或更多的国际学生，对于一些院校来说，这场危机可能是存在的。对整个美国社会的连锁反应也可能是毁灭性的：根据NAFSA的数据，美国每七个注册的国际学生就有三个就业机会被创造或支持在以下领域：高等教育、住宿、餐饮、零售、交通、电信和医疗保险。',
  'HOW COVID-19 HAS IMPACTED THE STUDY PLANS OF MOBILE STUDENTS' => 'COVID-19对流动学生学习计划的影响',
  'One positive takeaway from our survey is that many international students seem to view the coronavirus pandemic as a temporary phenomenon. A slight majority of 53 percent of respondents who intended to study in the U.S. before the pandemic plan to merely postpone their studies, rather than scrap their plans altogether or study at home or in another country. The fact that 23 percent of respondents are likely to study in a different country, however, should serve as a warning to U.S. institutions. Countries that bring pandemic spread under control the earliest will almost certainly have an advantage in recruiting mobile students once international mobility sputters back into gear.' => '我们调查的一个积极结论是，许多国际学生似乎将冠状病毒大流行视为一种暂时现象。在流感大流行前打算去美国学习的受访者中，有53%的人计划仅仅推迟他们的研究，而不是完全放弃他们的计划，或者在国内或其他国家学习。然而，23%的受访者可能会去另一个国家学习，这一事实应该对美国的教育机构起到警示作用。一旦国际流动性重新启动，那些最早控制疫情蔓延的国家几乎肯定在招收流动学生方面具有优势。',
  'The Australian government, for instance, currently plans to exempt international students from travel restrictions and allow them to return to Australia <a href="">as early as July</a> —a scenario that seems out of reach in the U.S. at this point. Similarly, observers believe that New Zealand, a country which has effectively <a href="">contained the pandemic</a>, will have “a real opportunity to become more desirable as a destination for <a href="">foreign students</a>” because of the crisis.' => '例如，澳大利亚政府目前计划免除国际学生的旅行限制，并允许他们最早在7月返回澳大利亚，这在美国看来是遥不可及的。同样，观察家认为，由于危机，新西兰作为一个有效地控制了这场大流行的国家，将有“一个真正的机会成为一个更受欢迎的留学生目的地”。',
  'The longer the image of the U.S. is tarnished by its pandemic response, a perceived strong risk of a second wave of infections, and increasingly harsh immigration restrictions, the harder it will be for U.S. HEIs to compete with academic institutions in other international education hubs. Fully 50 percent of students surveyed by WES anticipate that the coronavirus crisis will negatively impact the openness of U.S. society to international students.' => '美国的大流行反应、第二波感染的严重风险以及日益严厉的移民限制使美国的形象受损的时间越长，美国高等教育机构就越难与其他国际教育中心的学术机构竞争。WES调查的学生中，有整整50%的人预计冠状病毒危机将对美国社会对国际学生的开放产生负面影响。',
  'Equally disconcerting, if unsurprising, is the fact that 20 percent of prospective international students stated that they’re now likely to study in their home countries. This is a percentage that may well increase if the pandemic continues to drag on in the U.S. and other destination countries. Local surveys in India, cited in April by the <a href="">Hindustan Times</a> , found that more than half of Indian students who had intended to study abroad planned to cancel those plans, while about a third of them sought to defer existing offers of acceptance by a year. Indian recruitment agents forecast increased competition over scarce domestic university seats this year as previously outbound students now find themselves seeking options at home.' => '同样令人不安的是，20%的潜在留学生表示，他们现在有可能在本国学习。如果流感大流行在美国和其他目的地国家继续蔓延，这个比例很可能会增加。<a href=“”>印度斯坦时报4月援引印度当地的调查发现，超过一半的印度留学生计划取消这些计划，而其中约三分之一的人试图将现有的录取申请推迟一年。印度招生代理机构预测，今年国内大学席位的竞争将加剧，因为以前出国留学的学生现在发现自己在国内寻找选择。',
  'ECONOMIC CONCERNS' => '经济问题',
  'Aside from travel restrictions and safety concerns, financial constraints have become a greater barrier, with many parents and students now unable or unwilling to raise funds for an expensive international education amid constricting lockdowns and surging unemployment. Seventy-nine percent of prospective students surveyed by WES expect economic conditions in their home country to be negatively affected by the pandemic; 43 percent fear that they will no longer be able to afford studying in the United States.' => '除了旅行限制和安全问题外，经济拮据已成为一个更大的障碍，在紧缩的封锁和激增的失业率下，许多家长和学生现在无法或不愿为昂贵的国际教育筹集资金。WES调查的79%的准留学生预计本国的经济状况会受到流感大流行的负面影响；43%的人担心他们将无法负担在美国的学习费用。',
  'Whereas travel restrictions, office closures, and the suspension of mail services and tests like the SAT or TOEFL will inevitably disrupt international student admissions in the short term, a global recession will impede student mobility much more severely and long lastingly. Even though global outbound student mobility kept growing throughout the Great Recession, economic downturns do affect mobility quite significantly, particularly with respect to student flows from lower middle-income countries to high-cost study destinations. This can be seen in the following graphic, which illustrates a distinct drop in outbound mobility when India, the world’s second-largest sender of international students, experienced an economic crisis in the early 2010s.' => '尽管旅行限制、办公室关闭、邮件服务和SAT或托福考试的暂停将不可避免地在短期内扰乱国际学生的入学，但全球经济衰退将更严重、更持久地阻碍学生的流动。尽管在经济大萧条期间，全球留学生流动性一直在增长，但经济衰退确实对流动性产生了相当大的影响，尤其是从中等偏下收入国家流向高成本留学目的地的学生流动。这可以从下面的图表中看出，当世界第二大留学生输出国印度在20世纪10年代初经历经济危机时，出境流动性明显下降。',
  'The Trump administration’s plans to' => '特朗普政府计划',
  'suspend the OPT program' => '暂停OPT程序',
  ' are detrimental in this context. While other countries are weighing options to attract more international students, including by expanding <a href="">access to employment</a> , the Trump administration’s policies won’t help the U.S. hold on to its global share of the international student market, which has already declined by an estimated 6 percent since the beginning of <a href="">the century</a> . Independent of possible visa restrictions, the current unemployment rate of close to <a href="">15 percent</a> and the prospect of a protracted economic crisis mean that the U.S. will lose part of its sheen as a destination for students interested in employment and possibly immigration after graduation.' => '在这种情况下是有害的。虽然其他国家正在考虑各种办法来吸引更多的国际学生，包括扩大就业机会，但特朗普政府的政策无助于美国保住国际学生市场的全球份额，自本世纪初以来，估计已经下降了6%。不考虑可能的签证限制，目前接近15%的失业率和旷日持久的经济危机意味着美国将失去一部分对就业感兴趣的学生和毕业后移民感兴趣的学生的目的地。',
  'Given the catastrophic economic outlook for countries globally, some observers have suggested that it will take international student mobility five years to recover from <a href="">the pandemic</a>. While that forecast appears overly pessimistic, it’s all but certain that fewer students will head abroad for the foreseeable future as incomes and public scholarships dry up. Students from lower middle-income countries like India, Bangladesh, and Vietnam, all top sending countries of students to the U.S., may opt for less expensive study destinations that are closer to home, such as China, Malaysia, or South Korea. International branch campuses and transnational programs that allow students to obtain an international education without travel may become more popular.' => '鉴于全球各国面临灾难性的经济前景，一些观察家认为，国际学生流动需要五年时间才能从这场大流行中恢复过来。虽然这一预测显得过于悲观，但可以肯定的是，随着收入和公共奖学金的枯竭，在可预见的未来，前往国外留学的学生将减少。来自印度、孟加拉国和越南等中等偏下收入国家的学生可能会选择离家较近的较便宜的留学目的地，如中国、马来西亚或韩国。国际分校和跨国项目，允许学生在没有旅行的情况下接受国际教育，可能会变得更受欢迎。',
  'THE OUTLOOK FROM AN INSTITUTIONAL PERSPECTIVE' => '制度视角下的展望',
  'In sum, there’s reason for concern: 77 percent of HEIs surveyed by WES expect a downturn in international enrollments because of the crisis—a notable difference when compared to the Great Recession, which was accompanied by a significant <a href="">uptick in enrollments</a> by domestic and international students alike. Most HEIs—64 percent—are extremely concerned that travel restrictions may impede international student mobility and 70 percent worry that new international students will not be able to get a visa. Sixty-four percent predict that HEIs will consequently increase “backyard recruitment” of foreign-educated students already in the U.S. to compensate for the loss.' => '总而言之，我们有理由担心：在WES调查的高等教育机构中，77%的人预计国际入学率会因为危机而下降——与大萧条相比，这是一个显著的差异，而经济大衰退的同时，国内和国际学生的入学率也显著上升。大多数HEIs-64%的人非常担心旅行限制可能会阻碍国际学生的流动性，70%的人担心新来的国际学生将无法获得签证。64%的人预测高等教育学院将因此增加对已经在美国的外国留学生的“后院招聘”，以弥补损失。',
  'IS ONLINE EDUCATION A VIABLE ALTERNATIVE?' => '在线教育是否可行？',
  'Given the uncertainties as to when the pandemic will be contained, growing numbers of institutions are shifting to online education beyond the summer. As of this writing, <a href="">7 percent</a> of institutions have announced that they will deliver education online in the upcoming fall semester. Another 28 percent of HEIs, including major international host institutions like Columbia University and the University of Southern California, are still deciding or are considering other options, including blended learning. For international students unable to travel, distance learning will likely be more common: 52 percent of 234 U.S. HEIs polled in a <a href="">recent survey</a> by the Institute of International Education stated that they would provide online options for international students in the fall.' => '考虑到疫情何时得到控制的不确定性，越来越多的机构在暑期后转向在线教育。在撰写本文时，<a href=“”>7%的机构已经宣布他们将在即将到来的秋季学期提供在线教育。另外28%的高等教育机构，包括哥伦比亚大学和南加州大学等主要国际主办机构，仍在决定或正在考虑其他选择，包括混合学习。对于无法旅行的国际学生来说，远程学习可能更为普遍：在国际教育研究所（Institute of international Education）最近的一项调查中，234名美国高等教育学院（hei）中，52%的人表示，他们将在秋季为国际学生提供在线选择。',
  'Some observers have suggested that the rapid global shift toward distance learning may provide HEIs with a golden opportunity to reach more students overseas with online programs. Former U.K. higher education minister Jo Johnson, for instance, thinks that British universities will be able to increase overseas enrollments from lower “income groups in Asia and Africa where young people do not necessarily want the full-fat, high-cost, three- to four-year program living in an <a href="">English-speaking country</a>.”' => '一些观察家认为，全球向远程教育的快速转变可能为高等教育提供一个黄金机会，让更多的海外学生通过在线课程接触到他们。例如，前英国高等教育部长Jo Johnson认为，英国大学将能够从较低的“亚洲和非洲的收入群体”中增加海外入学率，在那里年轻人不一定需要全脂、高成本、三到四年的项目生活在<HREF=“”英语国家</A>。',
  'However, while there’s certainly the potential to reach more students in untapped overseas markets with distance education programs, there are doubts about how popular online options will actually be for international students, especially among students already enrolled in degree programs. Fully 32 percent of international students surveyed by WES said that they would not continue their studies in online mode, while another 30 percent were undecided. This finding mirrors the sentiments of domestic students: 33 percent of prospective U.S. students polled in May said that they would “defer or cancel their fall semester if schools go <a href="">totally online</a>.”' => '然而，尽管远程教育项目肯定有可能在未开发的海外市场上吸引更多的学生，但对于国际学生，尤其是已经注册了学位课程的学生来说，在线选项究竟会有多受欢迎，还是有疑问的。WES调查的国际学生中，有32%的人表示他们不会继续在线学习，另有30%的人还没有决定。这一发现反映了国内学生的情绪：5月份接受调查的美国学生中有33%表示，“如果学校完全在线，他们将推迟或取消秋季学期。”',
  'There are technical issues to consider as well. Several universities have reported difficulties delivering learning content to students in China because of internet censorship and the inaccessibility of popular <a href="">online platforms</a>. What’s more, it will be difficult to offer online programs at the same price as full-fledged on-campus programs, so the revenues of major host institutions would be at risk either way if education were to be delivered wholly online on a prolonged basis.' => '还有一些技术问题需要考虑。有几所大学报告说，由于互联网审查制度和无法使用流行的<a href=“”>在线平台</a>，在向中国学生提供学习内容方面存在困难。更重要的是，很难以与正式的校园课程相同的价格提供在线课程，因此，如果长期完全在线提供教育，主要主办机构的收入将面临风险。',
  'It remains an open question whether online education will help retain international students in the long run. While some students will certainly be put off by paying hefty fees for an international online education, some institutions and countries may stand to benefit. As one Canadian immigration policy analyst has noted, “international students who wish to eventually apply for Canadian immigration will want to capitalize on the opportunity to complete a portion of their studies in their countries of origin, while still being able to access the same benefits (the work permits) had they been required to physically study in Canada.… The cost to study in Canada will decline for them, since they will not have to incur additional living expenses at the outset of their <a href="">Canadian education</a>.”' => '从长远来看，在线教育是否有助于留住国际学生，这仍是一个未知数。虽然一些学生肯定会因为支付高额的国际在线教育费用而被推迟，但一些机构和国家可能会从中受益。正如一位加拿大移民政策分析员所指出的，“希望最终申请加拿大移民的国际学生将希望利用在原籍国完成部分学业的机会，如果他们被要求在加拿大进行物理学习，他们仍然能够获得相同的福利（工作许可证）……他们在加拿大学习的成本将下降，因为他们在开始接受加拿大教育时不必支付额外的生活费</a>',
  'For Context: Other Surveys' => '上下文：其他调查',
  'By and large, several of our survey findings are mirrored by those of other surveys. For example, <a href="">69 percent</a> of 6,900 international students recently surveyed by U.K.-based education consultants IDP Connect stated that they still intend to begin their studies as planned. Most of them prefer to do so on campus and defer their start dates if necessary, while a sizable number of respondents were unwilling to continue studies in online mode, expressing concerns about quality and noting that it “ lacked international exposure.” ' => '总的来说，我们的一些调查结果与其他调查结果相一致。例如，最近被英国教育顾问IDP Connect调查的6900名国际学生的“HREF＝”＞69%＜A/A>表示他们仍打算按计划开始学习。他们中的大多数人更愿意在校园里这样做，如果有必要的话推迟开学日期，而相当多的受访者不愿意继续在线学习，他们对学习质量表示担忧，并指出这“缺乏国际曝光度”',
  'While these attitudes might change over time, as the crisis continues to unfold, <a href="">32 percent</a> of prospective international students abroad surveyed by educations.com said they weren’t interested in continuing their studies in online mode. After surveying 22,000 international students, the Erasmus Student Network noted that while distance learning is an acceptable solution to an unprecedented problem ” … online classes are not a proper substitute for a physical mobility experience. Several problems were reported with the technical implementation of online courses, and while these can probably be worked around, the real ‘Erasmus experience’ is <a href="">unlikely to be the same</a> ”. As QS summarized its most recent <a href="">survey findings</a> , “international students may be deferred but they’re not deterred” from continuing their studies on campus should conditions permit.' => '虽然这些态度可能会随着时间的推移而改变，随着危机的持续发展，<a href=“”>32%</a>接受了教育网说他们对继续在线学习不感兴趣。伊拉斯谟学生网络在调查了22000名国际学生后指出，虽然远程学习是一个前所未有的问题的可接受的解决办法，但“在线课程并不能适当地替代物理移动体验。据报道，在线课程的技术实施存在一些问题，虽然这些问题可能可以解决，但真正的“伊拉斯谟体验”不太可能是相同的</a>。正如QS总结其最新的调查结果所述，“如果条件允许，国际学生可能会被推迟，但他们不会被阻止”继续在校园学习。',
  'MAJOR UNCERTAINTIES AHEAD' => '未来的主要不确定性',
  'While it’s difficult to see international student mobility fully rebound under the current circumstances, it needs to be understood that global student mobility has grown consistently and reliably over the past three decades, crises like the Great Recession or the SARS epidemic notwithstanding. Consider that between 2000 and 2017, the number of mobile students enrolled in degree programs in other countries more than doubled, from 2 million to 5.3 million, according to the latest available UNESCO statistics. Looking forward, the number of tertiary students worldwide is estimated to rise from 251 million in 2020 to 594 million <a href=""> by 2040</a>—making it all but certain that international student mobility will continue to increase, at least to some extent, in the long term.' => '虽然在目前的情况下，国际学生流动性很难完全反弹，但需要理解的是，在过去的三十年里，全球学生流动性一直在稳定、可靠地增长，尽管存在大衰退或非典疫情等危机。根据联合国教科文组织现有的最新统计数据，2000年至2017年期间，在其他国家就读学位课程的流动学生人数翻了一番多，从200万增加到530万。展望未来，预计到2040年，全球高等教育学生的数量将从2020年的2.51亿增加到5.94亿<a href=“”>这几乎可以肯定，从长期来看，国际学生流动性将继续增加，至少在某种程度上是如此。',
  'Past trends in the U.S., the most popular international study destination worldwide, show resilience to global crises as well. Aside from a brief period of stagnation in the early 2000s in the wake of the 9/11 terror attacks and the globally unpopular Iraq war, international student enrollments in the U.S. have been growing steadily, almost doubling between <a href="">2006 and 2017</a> .' => '作为全球最受欢迎的国际留学目的地，美国过去的趋势也显示出对全球危机的应变能力。除了9/11恐怖袭击和全球不受欢迎的伊拉克战争的影响，美国的国际学生入学率在21世纪初出现了短暂的停滞，在2006年至2017年间几乎翻了一番。',
  'At the same time, we are sailing in uncharted waters because of the global totality of the pandemic. There are many unanswered questions as the crisis continues to unfold. For instance, how will the education systems of major sending countries be transformed by the crisis? To what extent will private institutions outside of public safety nets go belly-up, and by how much will public university budgets be slashed? Such factors could limit access to education and consequently drive more students overseas.' => '与此同时，由于这一流行病的全球性，我们正在未知的水域航行。随着危机的持续发展，还有许多问题没有得到解答。例如，危机将如何改变主要输出国的教育体系？公共安全网之外的私立机构会在多大程度上破产，公立大学预算将削减多少？这些因素可能会限制受教育的机会，从而导致更多的学生出国。',
  'On the other hand, if the pandemic should be prolonged, will distance learning be mainstreamed and become more ubiquitous even at top institutions, potentially increasing access to education and widening bottlenecks, thereby easing pressures to pursue alternative study options abroad? If there is a prolonged shift to distance learning, will this change be broadly accepted, or will distance education still be considered second rate, with elites opting for on-campus programs that include real cultural immersion experiences abroad, rather than studying “canned content” in their bedrooms?' => '另一方面，如果这一流行病应该延长，远程教育是否会被纳入主流，甚至在顶尖院校也会变得更加普遍，从而可能增加受教育的机会并扩大瓶颈，从而减轻在国外寻求其他学习选择的压力？如果长期向远程教育转变，这种改变会被广泛接受吗，还是远程教育仍被视为二流，精英们会选择包括真正的海外文化沉浸体验的校园课程，而不是在卧室里学习“罐装内容”？',
  'Closer to home, will the presidential election in November result in a change of government, potentially ushering in an era of greater openness that could rekindle interest in the U.S. as a preferred international study destination?' => '在美国本土，11月的总统大选是否会导致政府更迭，从而可能带来一个更加开放的时代，从而重新激起人们对美国作为首选国际留学目的地的兴趣？',
  'With all these questions hanging in the balance, it’s difficult to predict how international student mobility to the U.S. will develop in the future. However, there are good reasons to believe that the current crisis may hasten the relative decline of the U.S. as an international study destination, going beyond a short-term crash. The number of Chinese students in the U.S.—already growing at a decelerated pace before the crisis—is likely to contract. We may well witness a greater regionalization of student mobility and shifts in student flows to other countries. Destination countries with efficient and socially compassionate epidemic control mechanisms and health care systems stand to gain from the crisis. While factors like the growing number of tertiary students worldwide and the global reputation of U.S. universities will ultimately continue to bring international students to the U.S., the country’s HEIs must brace themselves—now more than ever—for significant changes in international student flows.' => '在所有这些问题悬而未决的情况下，很难预测未来国际学生赴美流动的发展趋势。然而，有充分的理由相信，当前的危机可能会加速美国作为国际留学目的地的相对衰落，而不仅仅是短期的崩溃。在美国的中国留学生人数在危机爆发前已经以减速的速度增长，很可能会收缩。我们很可能会看到学生流动性的更大区域化和学生流向其他国家的转变。拥有高效和社会同情心的流行病控制机制和卫生保健系统的目的地国家将从这场危机中获益。尽管全球高等教育学生数量的不断增长以及美国大学的全球声誉等因素最终将继续把国际学生带到美国，但美国的高等教育机构现在必须比以往任何时候都更加坚定地面对国际学生流的重大变化。',
  'Job Opportunity' => '工作机会',
  'Online Education' => '在线教育',
  'Study Plan' => '学习计划',
  'COVID-19 Emergency Responses in Education' => 'COVID-19教育应急响应',
  'As of April 27th, 2020, the <a href="">International Credential Evaluation Service (ICES)</a> has made the online application available again and will be open to receiving requests for evaluations both online and by mail. The Covid-19 pandemic will still certainly affect business operations including disruptions to mail services in many countries (see below). If you are unable to get your institution to provide educational documents and have already applied or are thinking of applying, we can still hold your application until such documents arrive.' => '截至2020年4月27日，<a href=“”>国际认证评估服务（ICES）</a>已再次提供在线申请，并将接受在线和邮寄评估请求。Covid-19流感大流行仍将影响商业运作，包括许多国家的邮件服务中断（见下文）。如果您无法让您的机构提供教育文件，并且已经申请或正在考虑申请，我们仍然可以保留您的申请，直到这些文件到达。',
  'Disrupted mail service' => '邮件服务中断',
  'The Covid-19 pandemic has disrupted mail service both outgoing and incoming to many countries throughout the world. Some countries have suspended mail service altogether whereas in other areas it might be significantly delayed. ICES is not able to provide estimated delivery times for mail. If that is what you require, you may wish to contact your local postal service.' => 'Covid-19流感大流行已经扰乱了世界上许多国家的邮件收发服务。一些国家已经完全停止了邮件服务，而在其他地区，这一服务可能会大大推迟。ICES无法提供邮件的预计送达时间。如果这是您需要的，您可以联系您当地的邮政服务。',
  'Here’s the update from <a href="">Canada Post</a> , you can find specific information about disruptions in your <a href="">country</a> here.' => '这是来自<a href=“”>加拿大邮政的最新消息，您可以在这里找到有关您所在国家的中断的具体信息。',
  'Courier service is also impacted. Again, in some cases it has been suspended completely and in other cases there are severe delays. Also due to social distancing measures, there may be no signature requested at the time of delivery. For Domestic courier, please see the <a href="">UPS services alerts</a>. For International courier, please see the <a href="">DHL service alerts</a>. ICES is unable to provide estimated delivery times.' => '快递服务也受到影响。同样，在某些情况下，它被完全中止，在另一些情况下则出现严重延误。此外，由于社会距离措施，可能没有要求在交付时签名。对于国内快递，请参见<a href=“”>UPS服务提醒</a>。对于国际快递，请参见<a href=“”>DHL服务提醒</a>。ICES无法提供估计的交货时间。',
  'Mail and Courier Restrictions' => '邮件和快递限制',
  'Canada Post has suspended all mail services to Syria. Please see this notification of the <a href="">OFAC trade embargo</a> for more information. If you apply and your return address is in Syria, we will not be able to offer any mail or courier service. In this case, please provide an alternate address for the delivery of your assessment.' => '加拿大邮政已暂停所有前往叙利亚的邮件服务。有关更多信息，请参阅本OFAC贸易禁运通知。如果您申请并且您的回信地址在叙利亚，我们将无法提供任何邮件或快递服务。在这种情况下，请提供另一个地址，以便提交您的评估。',
  'International courier is suspended to the following countries:' => '暂停向以下国家提供国际快递服务：',
  'Cuba' => '古巴',
  'Iran' => '伊朗',
  'Kosovo' => '科索沃',
  'Kyrgyzstan' => '吉尔吉斯斯坦',
  'North Korea' => '朝鲜',
  'Somalia' => '索马里',
  'Sudan' => '苏丹',
  'Syria' => '叙利亚',
  'Turkmenistan' => '土库曼斯坦',
  'If you have applied and your return address is to one of the above countries, we will require an alternate address for delivery.' => '如果您已经申请，并且您的寄件地址是上述国家之一，我们将要求您提供另一个地址。',
  'ICES' => '冰',
  'Canada Post' => '加拿大邮政',
  'Perfect Storm:' => '完美风暴：',
  'This is a transcript of the presentation given during <a href="">Educause</a> at the Anaheim Convention Center on October 28, 2016.' => '这是2016年10月28日在阿纳海姆会议中心举行的<a href=“”>Educause</a>期间所做演讲的记录。',
  'Hello everyone. My name is Chris Jagers. I’m the CEO of <a href="">Learning Machine</a> , the software company that has been working with MIT over the last year to develop an open standard for blockchain certificates. I’ll be giving a short presentation about blockchain-based academic credentials, followed by a discussion with our panel and with all of you.' => '大家好。我叫克里斯·贾格斯。我是<a href=“”>Learning Machine</a>的首席执行官，这家软件公司去年一直与麻省理工学院合作开发区块链证书的开放标准。我将做一个关于基于区块链的学术证书的简短演示，然后与我们的小组和各位进行讨论。',
  'There’s been a lot of genuine excitement around using the blockchain within higher education (and beyond) because the promise is immense. The promise is that it will enable students to hold and share their own official records directly with others in a manner that is safe, tamper-proof, and trusted. We’re talking about degrees, transcripts, certifications, badges … everything. That is a really big deal.' => '在高等教育（甚至更高层次）中使用区块链确实让人兴奋不已，因为它的前景是巨大的。它的承诺是，它将使学生能够以安全、防篡改和可信的方式与他人直接持有和共享自己的官方记录。我们在谈论学位，成绩单，证书，徽章…所有的东西。这真是件大事。',
  'Before we dive into details that technology, let’s cover some background. Even though schools moved from sheepskin to digital records a while ago, schools are still acting as the sole record keepers for student information. If a student wants to access or share their official records, they have to engage in a slow, complicated, and often expensive process. And so, for the most part, those records aren’t used much after graduation, nor built upon.' => '在我们深入研究这项技术的细节之前，让我们先介绍一些背景知识。尽管不久前学校从羊皮变成了数字记录，但学校仍然是学生信息的唯一记录保存者。如果一个学生想要访问或分享他们的官方记录，他们必须参与一个缓慢、复杂、而且往往昂贵的过程。所以，在很大程度上，这些唱片在毕业后并没有被广泛使用，也没有建立起来。',
  'Additionally, education is changing. Online learning and competency-based programs are rising in popularity. And this is magnified by a rapidly growing number of accredited education providers that expand far beyond traditional schools. This is causing a proliferation of educational claims that are hard to manage and it raises many new questions, both in terms of policy and technology. And what I hope to explain today is how a new technical infrastructure has emerged that enables students to be part of the solution by acting as their own lifelong registrar.' => '此外，教育正在发生变化。在线学习和基于能力的课程越来越受欢迎。越来越多的认证教育机构远远超出了传统学校的范围，这一点得到了进一步扩大。这导致了难以管理的教育主张的激增，并在政策和技术方面提出了许多新问题。我今天希望解释的是，一种新的技术基础设施是如何出现的，它使学生能够成为解决方案的一部分，成为他们自己的终身登记员。',
  'Let’s start by looking at an example. A little over a year ago, the MIT Media Lab started an experiment for issuing some alumni digital certificates that could be validated using the Bitcoin blockchain. I say “experiment,” because it wasn’t ready to be safely released to the public, but it did illustrate how to use the blockchain as a notary for issuing certificates and verifying their authenticity.' => '让我们从一个例子开始。一年多前，麻省理工学院媒体实验室开始了一项实验，为一些校友颁发数字证书，这些证书可以使用比特币区块链进行验证。我之所以说“实验”，是因为它还没有准备好安全地向公众发布，但它确实说明了如何使用区块链作为公证人来签发证书并验证其真实性。',
  'The image above shows that verification process taking place, which involves checking MIT’s signature, checking that nothing has changed in the certificate itself, and checking that the certificate hasn’t expired or been revoked. Once all that checks out, which just takes a second, a verified status is displayed.' => '上图显示了正在进行的验证过程，包括检查麻省理工学院的签名，检查证书本身是否没有任何变化，以及检查证书是否过期或被吊销。一旦所有的检查完毕，只需一秒钟，就会显示一个已验证的状态。',
  'We’ve all heard funny stories of kids attempting to text photos of their official grades during the admissions process, but MIT’s prototype demonstrated how this new technology could actually secure that type of direct interaction for sharing official records.' => '我们都听说过一些有趣的故事，孩子们在录取过程中试图用短信发送他们的官方成绩照片，但麻省理工学院的原型展示了这项新技术如何能够确保这种直接的互动，从而分享官方记录。',
  'Let’s take a closer look at that prototype. The bottom of this slide represents the global blockchain database, which is basically a timeline of transactions. It is constituted by blocks of transactions that form one continuous chain. A blockchain. And because each new block builds upon the previous block, the entire chain is immutable. This is why it’s often referred to as a secure anchor of trust, because no government or private company can edit its history. And the schematic on top shows the core concept for logging certificate transactions.' => '让我们仔细看看这个原型。这张幻灯片的底部是全球区块链数据库，它基本上是一个交易时间轴。它由组成一个连续链的交易块组成。区块链。因为每个新的块都建立在前一个块的基础上，所以整个链是不可变的。这就是为什么它经常被称为可靠的信任之锚，因为没有任何政府或私人公司可以编辑它的历史。上面的示意图显示了记录证书事务的核心概念。',
  'The blockchain itself is simply a ledger of transactions. In the case of money, it is recording financial transactions: who sent it, who received it, and how much. That pattern makes it ideally suited to record academic credentialing as well, because it records the same basic things: who issued it, who received it, and a one-way hash of the content that can later be used for verification. An academic achievement is simply another kind of value.' => '区块链本身就是交易的账本。就钱而言，它记录的是金融交易：谁寄来的，谁收到的，以及金额。这种模式也使得它非常适合记录学术资格认证，因为它记录了相同的基本内容：谁颁发了证书，谁收到了证书，以及内容的单向散列，以后可以用于验证。学术成就只是另一种价值。',
  'The idea was clear, but this prototype had barriers preventing much use in the real world. For instance, it didn’t take into account how to efficiently issue thousands of certificates at the same time in a manner that was computationally efficient or cost effective. So, we began a year long collaboration to expand the concept and implementation into a complete toolkit of open-source components that any developer, school, or vendor could use.' => '这个想法很清楚，但是这个原型在现实世界中有很多阻碍。例如，它没有考虑到如何以计算效率或成本效益的方式同时有效地颁发数千个证书。因此，我们开始了长达一年的合作，将概念和实现扩展到一个完整的开源组件工具包中，任何开发人员、学校或供应商都可以使用。',
  'This week, we’re excited to announce that this toolkit has been launched and is freely available at <a href="">www.blockcerts.org</a>. This open standard is OBI compliant and includes libraries for creating, issuing, holding, viewing, and verifying blockchain credentials. There is no other public resource delivering this complete ecosystem. The website itself is a friendly introduction to the source code on Git, and it includes helpful articles that introduce the project, answers questions, and provides step-by-step guides.' => '本周，我们很高兴地宣布，这个工具包已经发布，并且可以在<a href=“”>www.blockcerts.org</a>。这个开放标准符合OBI，包括用于创建、发布、保存、查看和验证区块链凭证的库。没有其他公共资源能提供这个完整的生态系统。该网站本身是对Git上源代码的友好介绍，其中包括介绍项目、回答问题和提供分步指南的有用文章。',
  'And I should point out, that this codebase is already being used by MIT and others, so the future is here. It’s not two years away.' => '我应该指出，这个代码库已经被麻省理工学院和其他人使用，所以未来就在这里。不到两年了。',
  'Now, let’s take a look at how all these components can work together in the real world. This diagram is organized into three lanes: one for a school, one for a student, and one for employers or anyone else that needs to verify authenticity.' => '现在，让我们看看所有这些组件如何在现实世界中协同工作。这个图表被组织成三个通道：一个用于学校，一个用于学生，一个用于雇主或其他需要验证真实性的人。',
  'The process starts with the mobile app, which handles all of the crypto key-management stuff in the background. And just as you might add friends within a new app, the student simply adds their school. This sends the school their name, email, and public key which establishes a strong connection between them. Once that’s setup, the school can begin issuing that person certificates.' => '这个过程从移动应用程序开始，它在后台处理所有加密密钥管理工作。就像你可以在一个新的应用程序中添加朋友一样，学生只需添加他们的学校。这将向学校发送他们的姓名、电子邮件和公钥，从而在他们之间建立起一个牢固的联系。一旦设置好了，学校就可以开始颁发证书了。',
  'When a certificate is issued, a record of the transaction goes onto the blockchain. And the student can then hold their official certificate within their mobile app. The school still has an official copy, but now the student does as well.' => '当颁发证书时，交易记录进入区块链。学生可以在他们的移动应用程序中持有官方证书。学校仍然有官方版本，但现在学生也有了。',
  'Let’s say that student later wants to apply for a job. They apply through an employer’s HR system and they paste a link to their certificate. The HR system uses an independent blockchain verification service to verify any claims that are made. And it’s by using an independent verification service, as oppose to the one built into the certificate, that sidesteps any attempts at faking a blockchain certificate.' => '假设那个学生后来想申请一份工作。他们通过雇主的人力资源系统申请，并在证书上粘贴一个链接。人力资源系统使用独立的区块链验证服务来验证所提出的任何索赔。它通过使用一个独立的验证服务，而不是内置在证书中的服务，来避免任何伪造区块链证书的企图。',
  'That’s it. No school, vendor, or institution has to be consulted at any point during the verification process. The student has a convenient way to use their academic credentials, and employers have an immediate way to view and verify those claims. And perhaps more profoundly, the world has an entirely new infrastructure of trust for the 21st century.' => '就这样。在验证过程中，任何时候都不必咨询学校、供应商或机构。学生有一个方便的方式使用他们的学历证书，雇主有一个即时的方式来查看和核实这些索赔。或许更深刻的是，21世纪的世界有一个全新的信任基础设施。',
  'So let’s talk a little more about that infrastructure. The Bitcoin blockchain persists as a distributed network all over the world, just like the Internet. It’s replicated across thousands of computers, so it can’t be easily taken down. If institutions disappear, or even if entire governments collapse, people with blockchain-based certificates can still prove their education and what they have achieved. In essence, they can prove who they are. And the current refugee crisis highlights the relevance of this breakthrough. People need a more reliable ways to operate as self-sovereign individuals.' => '所以让我们再多谈一下这个基础设施。比特币区块链就像互联网一样，在全世界都是一个分布式网络。它可以在数千台计算机上复制，所以不容易被删除。如果机构消失，甚至整个政府崩溃，拥有区块链证书的人仍然可以证明他们的教育和他们取得的成就。本质上，他们可以证明他们是谁。而目前的难民危机凸显了这一突破的现实意义。人们需要一种更可靠的方式来作为自我主权的个体运作。',
  'In my experience, once schools grasp the magnitude of this technology, they want to get practical. How can they use it? How easy is it to get started?' => '以我的经验，一旦学校掌握了这项技术的重要性，他们就想变得实用。他们如何使用它？开始有多容易？',
  'If you’re a developer, the code and instructions for building are available today at blockcerts.org. If you’re school that wants a convenient product, we’ll be launching a commercial app for Registrars this January, which provides a graphical interface for issuing and tracking the use of certificates. This commercial product will also serve as a model to other vendors, for how they can use the Blockcerts toolkit to build out their own solutions.' => '如果您是一名开发人员，现在可以在blockcerts.org网站. 如果你的学校想要一个方便的产品，我们将在今年1月推出一个面向注册商的商业应用程序，它提供一个图形界面来发布和跟踪证书的使用情况。这一商业产品也将成为其他供应商的一个榜样，帮助他们如何使用Blockcerts工具箱构建自己的解决方案。',
  'And, I want to show you a preview of the product, because I think that seeing a friendly user interface can also help to clarify many of these concepts.' => '我想给大家展示一下这个产品的预览，因为我认为看到一个友好的用户界面也有助于澄清其中的许多概念。',
  'This particular view is part of the process for issuing a certificate template to an entire cohort of students. It’s kind of like an email campaign. At this point, the certificate on the right has been defined, the recipient list can be selected, the date/time of issuance can be scheduled, and the email notification can be customized as well. Once this goes out, the transaction gets registered on the the blockchain and the certificate appears for students in their mobile app. Image for post' => '此特定视图是向整个学生组颁发证书模板的过程的一部分。这有点像电子邮件宣传。此时，右侧的证书已经定义，可以选择收件人列表，可以安排颁发日期/时间，还可以自定义电子邮件通知。一旦这一点消失，交易就会在区块链上注册，学生的移动应用程序中就会出现证书。用于post的图像',
  'That’s what we’re looking at now above. Certificates are organized by school, which could include corporate training, alternative schools or any type of education provider. Individual certificates can be viewed and ultimately shared publicly online or privately with a third party. While issuing and verification happens via the bitcoin network, the certificate can also be displayed on the web, which generates the normal kinds of web analytics, like clicks and views.' => '这就是我们现在看到的。证书由学校组织，包括企业培训、替代学校或任何类型的教育提供者。个人证书可以在网上公开或私下与第三方共享。在通过比特币网络进行签发和验证的同时，证书也可以显示在网络上，这会产生正常的网络分析，如点击和浏览。',
  'So, coming back to the school’s view above, we’re now looking at a dashboard for the Advanced Robotics certificate where activity data is visualized. This provides schools a whole new layer of analytics that have never existed before. And these analytics could greatly be expanded should schools utilize some known taxonomy or credential registry. That data could be built into each certificate automatically resulting in more detailed analytics.' => '所以，回到学校的观点，我们现在看到的是高级机器人证书的仪表板，在那里活动数据是可视化的。这为学校提供了一个前所未有的全新的分析层面。如果学校使用一些已知的分类法或证书注册，这些分析可以大大扩展。这些数据可以自动内置到每个证书中，从而产生更详细的分析。',
  'This is obviously beneficial for everyone involved. First, it gives graduates a useful tool that directly contributes to their economic advancement. And by using a school’s branded certificates, it creates a daily reminder of the school in the mind of graduates and in the mind of others who are viewing certificates. So certificates become a type of marketing. And more importantly, the school and student maintain a connection that’s alive, far after graduation. And that ongoing connection has a lot of potential.' => '这显然对所有参与其中的人都是有益的。首先，它为毕业生提供了一个有用的工具，直接有助于他们的经济发展。通过使用学校的品牌证书，它在毕业生和其他正在查看证书的人的脑海中，每天都会想起学校。因此，证书成为一种营销方式。更重要的是，学校和学生在毕业后很长一段时间里保持着联系。这种持续的联系有很大的潜力。',
  'So, hopefully that’s enough to kick off good conversation!' => '所以，希望这足以开启一段美好的对话！',
  '...' => '...',
  'The presentation was followed by 45 minutes of great questions, most revolving around logistics like lost certificates, the longevity of the Bitcoin blockchain, and how employers adopt the verification service. Overall, a great discussion and enthusiasm for this direction.' => '演讲结束后，有45分钟的精彩提问，大部分围绕物流问题展开，比如丢失证书、比特币区块链的寿命以及雇主如何采用验证服务。总的来说，这个方向的讨论和热情高涨。',
  'Blockchain' => '块链',
  'Bitcoin' => '比特币',
  'Higher Education' => '高等教育',
  'Technology' => '技术',
  'Learning' => '学习',
  'For the last 100 years, a simple report called the academic transcript has operated as the official representation of student achievement. This bare-bones list of classes and grades was intended to facilitate communication between schools in an industrial age where the “traditional” student meant qualified 18–23 year olds who were enrolled full-time, residing on campus, and having their progress measured by time-exposure to subject matter via the credit hour (the Carnegie Unit).' => '在过去的100年里，一份名为“学业成绩单”的简单报告一直是学生成绩的官方代表。这个简单的班级和年级列表旨在促进工业时代的学校之间的交流，在工业时代，“传统”学生指的是合格的18-23岁的学生，他们全日制入学，居住在校园内，通过学时（卡内基单元）对学科的时间接触来衡量他们的进步。',
  'Those days are long gone.' => '那些日子早就过去了。',
  '<a href="">Analysis from 2011</a> summarizes less than one-quarter of all enrollment in higher education was at a four-year institution, and that percentage has been rapidly shrinking. Further, only half of those entrants into college are finishing. The rest are leaving with debt, no degree, and no other record with social value. Beyond the financial difficulty — for both students and schools — this trend is also creating new conceptions about what higher education should be. Rather than being a place for a select few to explore identity and possibly find a career, the model has flipped. Broad access is now considered a virtue and school is viewed increasingly as a pathway to a better job. And with so few attaining a degree, the idea of not finishing college has become the norm. The response to this mismatch between student expectations and academic options has been slow, not only because institutions are inherently slow to change, but also because the diverse growing numerical majority of non-traditional students has often been eclipsed by a lingering idealization of “traditional” students.' => '<a href=“”>2011年的分析总结出，在四年制高等教育机构就读的学生不到四分之一，而且这一比例正在迅速缩小。此外，只有一半的进入大学的学生完成学业。剩下的人则背负着债务，没有学位，也没有其他具有社会价值的记录。除了对学生和学校来说的财政困难之外，这一趋势也在创造新的高等教育理念。这一模式已经发生了转变，而不是成为少数人探索身份并可能找到职业的地方。广泛的就业机会现在被认为是一种美德，而学校也越来越被视为获得更好工作的途径。而且由于获得学位的人数很少，不完成大学学业的想法已经成为一种常态。对学生期望值与学业选择之间的这种不匹配的反应一直很慢，这不仅是因为学校本身的变化缓慢，而且还因为对“传统”学生的理想化挥之不去，使得数量上日益多样化的大多数非传统学生黯然失色。',
  'Today, school systems understand this trend and are actively responding.' => '今天，学校系统了解这一趋势并积极应对。',
  'First, there has been broad acknowledgment that time exposure to a subject doesn’t matter so much as actual skills achieved. In a <a href="">2015 report</a>, the Carnegie Foundation put it this way:' => '首先，人们普遍承认，接触一门学科的时间并不比掌握实际技能更重要。在a<a href=“”>2015年报告中，卡内基基金会这样说：',
  '“The Carnegie unit sought to standardize student exposure to subject matter by insuring they received consistent amounts of instructional time. It was never intended to function as a measure of what students learned.”' => '“卡内基小组试图通过确保学生获得一致的教学时间来规范学生对主题的接触。它从未打算作为衡量学生所学知识的标准。”',
  'The challenge for schools is that the Carnegie Unit has always been the organizing principle behind the academic transcript. Rethinking how academic experience gets documented requires a generous sense of mission that seeks out how to recognize learning in all of its variety. The ultimate desire is to evolve educational offerings and academic records in a way that helps three different stakeholders:' => '学校面临的挑战是，卡内基单元一直是学术成绩单背后的组织原则。重新思考学术经验是如何被记录下来的，需要一种慷慨的使命感，去寻找如何认识到学习的各种各样。最终的愿望是以一种有助于三个不同利益相关者的方式发展教育产品和学术记录：',
  '<b>Students: </b> how can academic records become part of the educational experience and remain an ongoing resource to the student?' => '<b>学生：</b>学习成绩如何成为教育经验的一部分，并成为学生的持续资源？',
  '<b>Employers: </b> how can academic records become more useful for hiring?' => '<b>雇主：</b>怎样才能使学术记录对招聘更有帮助？',
  '<b>Schools: </b> how can they record more kinds of learning experiences without diluting what an education means and without losing common understandings of achievement?' => '<b>学校：</b>他们如何记录更多的学习经验，而不削弱教育的意义，又不丧失对成就的共同理解？',
  'I was fortunate to be invited to this year’s meeting about the <a href="">Comprehensive Student Record</a> , hosted by the Lumina Foundation, which brought together leadership from schools from all over the U.S. to share their experiments for developing a more complete student record. Below are the dominant trends I observed, along with how securing records using the blockchain is directly aligned with strategic goals and serves all three stakeholder groups identified above.' => '我很幸运地被邀请参加今年由Lumina基金会主办的关于<a href=“”>综合学生档案的会议，该基金会汇集了来自美国各地的学校的领导，分享他们开发更完整学生记录的实验。以下是我观察到的主要趋势，以及使用区块链保护记录如何直接与战略目标保持一致，并为上述三个利益相关者群体提供服务。',
  'More Options for Certified Achievement' => '认证成就的更多选择',
  '<a href="">Steven Mintz</a>, Executive Director of the University of Texas System’s Institute for Transformational Learning, confirmed that that the University of Texas system has a 49% completion rate of students who finish with a degree, which mirrors national trends. In his beacon call about the state of education, <a href="">Navigating the Perfect Storm</a> , he argues that without smaller units of academic achievement as options, many students simply leave with debt. Universities are responding by offering various kinds of certificate programs and online courses that create flexible pathways for working and remote students. ASU’s <a href="">Global Freshman Academy</a> is a great example of these priorities put into practice.' => '<a href=“”>德克萨斯大学转型学习研究所的执行董事史蒂文·明茨（Steven Mintz）证实，德克萨斯大学系统拥有49%的完成率，这反映了全国的趋势。在他关于教育状况的指路明灯呼吁中，<a href=“”>在完美风暴中航行</a>，他认为，如果没有较小的学术成就单位作为选择，许多学生只会带着债务离开。各大学纷纷推出各种证书课程和在线课程，为在职和远程学生提供灵活的途径。ASU的<a href=“”>全球新生学院</a>就是这些优先事项付诸实践的一个很好的例子。',
  'Stanford University Registrar <a href="">Tom Black</a> shared their draft framework for organizing the 100+ certificate programs that are now being offered. It serves as a great example of how traditional universities can plan, organize, and prioritize their certificate programs.' => '斯坦福大学注册主任<a href=“”>Tom Black</a>分享了他们组织目前提供的100多个证书课程的框架草案。这是一个很好的例子，说明传统大学如何规划、组织和优先安排证书项目。',
  'At the base of this pyramid are open classes which simply confirm participation. These are low-stakes events that don’t require identity verification, but can be helpful to those who have attended. Moving up the pyramid means classes have greater academic rigor. The middle section shows different types of certifications for which identity is verified: Completion, Achievement, and Professional Certifications. Finally, the top level shown in gold represents official Stanford credit. This includes various undergraduate and graduate certificates, as well as the pinnacle of achievement — the university degree.' => '在金字塔的底部是公开课，它们只是确认参与。这些都是低风险的活动，不需要身份验证，但可以帮助那些参加过的人。往金字塔上爬意味着班级在学术上有更严格的要求。中间部分显示了身份验证的不同类型的证书：完成证书、成就证书和专业证书。最后，以黄金显示的最高级别代表斯坦福大学的官方学分。这包括各种本科和研究生证书，以及成就的顶峰——大学学位。',
  'Breaking up achievements and organizing them into a hierarchy gives students the option to pursue education at the level most appropriate for them. And by giving official certificates from Stanford, students receive a document that has personal and social value.' => '将成绩分解并组织成一个等级，学生可以选择在最适合他们的水平上接受教育。通过提供斯坦福大学的官方证书，学生们将获得一份具有个人和社会价值的文件。',
  'New Content and Formats' => '新内容和格式',
  'Many initiatives are seeking to revitalize the traditional academic transcript by growing their content and format in ways that address a desire for greater clarity about how coursework maps to actual competencies. Schools are addressing this need with two primary strategies:' => '许多倡议都在寻求振兴传统的学业成绩单，通过增加其内容和格式的方式，以满足对课程如何映射到实际能力的更清晰的渴望。学校通过两个主要策略来满足这一需求：',
  '<b>Enriching digital documents: </b> Rather than simply making what was once a paper document digital (generally a PDF), building rich documents that are linked to course descriptions, coursework, projects, etc.' => '<b>丰富数字文档：</b>而不是简单地将曾经的纸质文档数字化（通常是PDF），而是构建与课程描述、课程作业、项目等相关联的丰富文档。',
  '<b>Adding a co-curricular transcript: </b> These include lists of experiences, achievements, and competencies that have been earned outside of the classroom. Of course, this project raises many important questions about academic “equivalence” and practical concerns over the complexity of an undertaking with a transnational scope.' => '<b>增加一份课外成绩单：</b>这些包括在课堂之外获得的经验、成就和能力列表。当然，这个项目提出了许多关于学术“等效性”的重要问题，以及对跨国企业复杂性的实际关注。',
  'The pilot projects presented by nine different schools were presented with a larger aim to “capture learning wherever it occurs” and to issue evidence of those achievements in a manner that “belongs to the learner.” The Comprehensive Student Record (CSR), sometimes called the Lifelong Learning Record (LLR), is intended to fulfill both of those aims. Regardless of the challenges, the impetus for complete documentation of learning will require systems that can easily provide authoritative verification for every stakeholder. That is where the blockchain comes in.' => '由9所不同学校提出的试点项目的目的更大，即“在任何地方学习”，并以“属于学习者”的方式发布这些成就的证据。综合学生记录（CSR），有时称为终身学习记录（LLR），旨在实现这两个目标。不管有什么挑战，要想推动学习的完整文档化，就需要有一个系统能够轻松地为每个涉众提供权威的验证。这就是区块链的用武之地。',
  'Blockchain-Based Records' => '基于区块链的记录',
  'Broad agreement has emerged that whatever official records end up being produced, they should be owned by the learner. In the context of building a lifelong transcript of achievements and skills, I believe that ownership has to be literal — meaning learners must technically possess their records without any kind of ongoing dependence on institutions to certify them as authentic. Having to rely on every school, employer, club, and organization to provide official records over and over, across a lifetime, isn’t a realistic expectation. Plus, schools and other organizations may close. Learners must be able hold and share their official records directly with others in a manner that is trusted, even if the issuing institution has ceased to exist.' => '广泛的共识是，无论最终产生什么样的官方记录，它们都应该归学习者所有。在建立成就和技能的终身成绩单的背景下，我认为所有权必须是字面意思，即学习者必须在技术上拥有他们的记录，而不需要任何形式的持续依赖机构来证明他们是真实的。必须依赖每一所学校、雇主、俱乐部和组织在一生中不断提供官方记录，这不是一个现实的期望。另外，学校和其他组织可能会关闭。如果一个官方的学习者已经不能直接和其他人分享他们的记录，那么即使他们的记录已经不存在了。',
  'Is this technically possible? Yes.' => '这在技术上可行吗？对。',
  'The public blockchain is a world-wide network that maintains an immutable ledger of transactions. While that ledger has been used to record financial transactions for the past 10 years (Bitcoin), that same decentralized network can be used to store transactions of academic achievement. For example, MIT gave Sally this certificate. By using the blockchain as a notary, official documents can be shared peer-to-peer and independently verified as authentic. The blockchain doesn’t store or reveal student information, it simply stores a cryptographic receipt of the transaction. And that receipt can be independently cross-referenced anytime a student presents a claim of achievement to the world. If the receipt contained in the certificate matches the information on the blockchain, the claim is verified.' => '公共区块链是一个全球性的网络，它维护着一个不可变的交易账本。尽管过去10年来，该账本一直用于记录金融交易（比特币），但同样的分散网络也可以用于存储学术成就交易。例如，麻省理工学院给了莎莉这个证书。通过使用区块链作为公证人，可以对等共享官方文档，并独立验证其真实性。区块链不存储或透露学生信息，它只是存储交易的加密收据。当学生向全世界展示自己的成就时，这张收据可以独立地相互参照。如果证书中包含的收据与区块链上的信息相匹配，则验证索赔。',
  'The blockchain is a fundamental technology poised to be woven into our social infrastructure over the coming decade.' => '区块链是一项基础技术，将在未来十年内融入我们的社会基础设施。',
  'Further, all of the traditional and non-traditional documents being issued by schools can now be encoded in a standards-based way (diplomas, certificates, badges, transcripts, and the like) using Blockcerts. This is a set of standards for interacting with the public blockchain that allows each school to issue records of achievement that learners can actually possess and use in the real world. In short, this is how schools can contribute their part to a learner-owned CSR.' => '此外，学校签发的所有传统和非传统文件现在都可以使用区块证书以基于标准的方式（文凭、证书、徽章、成绩单等）进行编码。这是一套与公共区块链交互的标准，允许每个学校发布学习者在现实世界中实际拥有和使用的成绩记录。简而言之，这就是学校如何为学习者拥有的企业社会责任做出贡献。',
  'The only entity capable of truly assembling a comprehensive student record is the student.' => '唯一能够真正汇编完整学生档案的实体是学生。',
  'The movement to modularize education into smaller units of achievement, along with the innovation of a public blockchain to notarize those achievements, together constitute a secular shift in how learning is conceived and practiced. Giving students verifiable certificates for demonstrated competencies and completed coursework creates the gravitas needed to formally recognize achievements in a more granular way.' => '将教育模块化为较小的成就单元的运动，以及公证这些成就的公共区块链的创新，共同构成了学习构想和实践方式的长期转变。为学生提供证明能力和完成课程的可验证证书，创造了以更精细的方式正式认可成就所需的庄重感。',
  'The main benefit of blockchain-based digital records is that they are tamper-proof and independently verifiable. That means recipients can share their certificates online or directly with a potential employer via an Applicant Tracking System, and any claims can be automatically verified by checking the blockchain. No third party or school involvement is required to transmit official documents. Employers get the immediate confidence that everything being represented is true, and that convenience and extends to schools as well. When a student applies to a new school or transfers between schools, these digital certificates eliminate the arduous process of gathering official records from original sources.' => '基于区块链的数字记录的主要好处是它们是防篡改和独立验证的。这意味着接收者可以通过申请人跟踪系统在线或直接与潜在雇主共享证书，任何索赔都可以通过检查区块链自动验证。传递官方文件不需要第三方或学校参与。雇主们立竿见影地相信，所代表的一切都是真实的，而且方便也延伸到学校。当学生申请一所新学校或在学校之间转学时，这些数字证书消除了从原始来源收集官方记录的繁重过程。',
  'This new technology is the lynchpin that allows academic records to truly be learner-owned, and in turn, these create the perfect compliment to wider efforts already underway to make digital records more useful to students, employers, and schools.' => '这项新技术是一项关键技术，它允许学习者真正拥有学术记录，而反过来，这些技术又为使数字记录对学生、雇主和学校更有用而进行的更广泛的努力形成了完美的补充。',
  'Any school genuinely interested in enabling a CSR/LLR should be investigating how to utilize the public blockchain as a notary. <a href="">Blockcerts</a> provides the open-standard for interfacing with the blockchain and vendors like <a href="">Learning Machine</a> are building commercial solutions that utilize the standard in supported, scalable, cost-effective ways. A summative academic or co-curricular transcript may also be part of that record, but those are just one more stop on a lifelong journey of learning. Image for post' => '任何真正有兴趣实现CSR/LLR的学校都应该研究如何利用公共区块链作为公证人。<a href=“”>Blockcerts</a>提供了与区块链接口的开放标准，<a href=“”>Learning Machine</a>等供应商正在构建商业解决方案，以支持、可扩展、经济高效的方式利用该标准。一份总结性的学术或课外成绩单也可能是这一记录的一部分，但这些只是终身学习旅程中的又一站。用于post的图像',
  'Please click the ♡ below to support individuals owning their own official records and building a lifelong record that they can control.' => '请单击下面的♡以支持个人拥有自己的官方记录，并建立一个他们可以控制的终身记录。',
